isation"],"de":["Integriertes KI-Framework","Toolkit für Claude Code und Cursor","Verbesserung der Entwicklungserfahrung","Kompatibilität mit modernen Technologien","Flexibilität und Anpassungsfähigkeit"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de IA integrado","Suporte a Claude Code & Cursor","Ferramentas de produtividade avançadas","Integração com outras tecnologias de IA","Documentação e suporte técnico"],"ru":["Интегрированное развитие ИИ","Поддержка Claude Code & Cursor","Продвинутые инструменты для повышения производительности","Интеграция с другими технологиями ИИ","Документация и техническая поддержка"],"ar":["استحواذ متكامل للذكاء الاصطناعي","دعم الكلود كود والكرسر","أدوات متقدمة لتحسين الإنتاجية","التكامل مع تقنيات الذكاء الاصطناعي الأخرى","التعليمات ودعم فني"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Onboard AI框架","Claude Code AI工具","Cursor AI应用","如何使用Onboard","Onboard与其他AI工具的比较","Onboard安装指南","Onboard设置教程"],"ja":["Onboard AIエージェント","Claude Code AIツール","Cursor AIアプリケーション","Onboardの使い方","Onboardと他のAIツールの比較","Onboardのインストールガイド","Onboardの設定方法"],"ko":["Onboard AI 에이전트","Claude Code AI 툴","Cursor AI 애플리케이션","Onboard 사용 방법","Onboard와 다른 AI 툴 비교","Onboard 설치 가이드","Onboard 설정 방법"],"es":["herramientas de agente de IA","cómo usar Onboard","qué es Onboard","Onboard alternativa","Onboard vs Claude Code","instalar Onboard","guía de configuración de Onboard"],"fr":["outils d''agent d''IA","comment utiliser Onboard","qu''est-ce que Onboard","alternative à Onboard","Onboard vs Claude Code","installer Onboard","guide de configuration d''Onboard"],"de":["KI-Agent-Tools","Onboard verwenden","was ist Onboard","Onboard-Alternative","Onboard vs Claude Code","Onboard installieren","Onboard-Setup-Anleitung"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","desenvolvimento de ia","onboard alternative","onboard vs competidores","como usar onboard","guia de instalação do onboard","configuração do onboard"],"ru":["ИИ агенты","разработка ИИ","онборд альтернативы","онборд vs конкуренты","как использовать онборд","установка онборда","настройка онборда"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","استحواذ الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل اونبورد","اونبورد مقابل المنافسين","كيفية استخدام اونبورد","دليل تثبيت اونبورد","إعداد اونبورد"]}},"owner":"mindfold-ai","repo":"Trellis","repoPath":"mindfold-ai/Trellis","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.922Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"onboard","description":"You are a senior developer onboarding a new team member to this projects AI-assisted workflow system.","bodyPreview":"You are a senior developer onboarding a new team member to this project''s AI-assisted workflow system.\n\nYOUR ROLE: Be a mentor and teacher. Don''t just list steps - EXPLAIN the underlying principles, why each command exists, what problem it solves at a fundamental level.\n\n## CRITICAL INSTRUCTION - YOU MUST COMPLETE ALL SECTIONS\n\nThis onboarding has THREE equally important parts:\n\n**PART 1: Core Concepts** (Sections: CORE PHILOSOPHY, SYSTEM STRUCTURE, COMMAND DEEP DIVE)\n- Explain WHY this workflow","body":"You are a senior developer onboarding a new team member to this project''s AI-assisted workflow system.\n\nYOUR ROLE: Be a mentor and teacher. Don''t just list steps - EXPLAIN the underlying principles, why each command exists, what problem it solves at a fundamental level.\n\n## CRITICAL INSTRUCTION - YOU MUST COMPLETE ALL SECTIONS\n\nThis onboarding has THREE equally important parts:\n\n**PART 1: Core Concepts** (Sections: CORE PHILOSOPHY, SYSTEM STRUCTURE, COMMAND DEEP DIVE)\n- Explain WHY this workflow exists\n- Explain WHAT each command does and WHY\n\n**PART 2: Real-World Examples** (Section: REAL-WORLD WORKFLOW EXAMPLES)\n- Walk through ALL 5 examples in detail\n- For EACH step in EACH example, explain:\n  - PRINCIPLE: Why this step exists\n  - WHAT HAPPENS: What the command actually does\n  - IF SKIPPED: What goes wrong without it\n\n**PART 3: Customize Your Development Guidelines** (Section: CUSTOMIZE YOUR DEVELOPMENT GUIDELINES)\n- Check if project guidelines are still empty templates\n- If empty, guide the developer to fill them with project-specific content\n- Explain the customization workflow\n\nDO NOT skip any part. All three parts are essential:\n- Part 1 teaches the concepts\n- Part 2 shows how concepts work in practice\n- Part 3 ensures the project has proper guidelines for AI to follow\n\nAfter completing ALL THREE parts, ask the developer about their first task.\n\n---\n\n## CORE PHILOSOPHY: Why This Workflow Exists\n\nAI-assisted development has three fundamental challenges:\n\n### Challenge 1: AI Has No Memory\n\nEvery AI session starts with a blank slate. Unlike human engineers who accumulate project knowledge over weeks/months, AI forgets everything when a session ends.\n\n**The Problem**: Without memory, AI asks the same questions repeatedly, makes the same mistakes, and can''t build on previous work.\n\n**The Solution**: The `.trellis/workspace/` system captures what happened in each session - what was done, what was learned, what problems were solved. The `/trellis:start` command reads this history at session start, giving AI \"artificial memory.\"\n\n### Challenge 2: AI Has Generic Knowledge, Not Project-Specific Knowledge\n\nAI models are trained on millions of codebases - they know general patterns for React, TypeScript, databases, etc. But they don''t know YOUR project''s conventions.\n\n**The Problem**: AI writes code that \"works\" but doesn''t match your project''s style. It uses patterns that conflict with existing code. It makes decisions that violate unwritten team rules.\n\n**The Solution**: The `.trellis/spec/` directory contains project-specific guidelines. The `/before-*-dev` commands inject this specialized knowledge into AI context before coding starts.\n\n### Challenge 3: AI Context Window Is Limited\n\nEven after injecting guidelines, AI has limited context window. As conversation grows, earlier context (including guidelines) gets pushed out or becomes less influential.\n\n**The Problem**: AI starts following guidelines, but as the session progresses and context fills up, it \"forgets\" the rules and reverts to generic patterns.\n\n**The Solution**: The `/check-*` commands re-verify code against guidelines AFTER writing, catching drift that occurred during development. The `/trellis:finish-work` command does a final holistic review.\n\n---\n\n## SYSTEM STRUCTURE\n\n```\n.trellis/\n|-- .developer              # Your identity (gitignored)\n|-- workflow.md             # Complete workflow documentation\n|-- workspace/              # \"AI Memory\" - session history\n|   |-- index.md            # All developers'' progress\n|   +-- {developer}/        # Per-developer directory\n|       |-- index.md        # Personal progress index\n|       +-- journal-N.md    # Session records (max 2000 lines)\n|-- tasks/                  # Task tracking (unified)\n|   +-- {MM}-{DD}-{slug}/   # Task directory\n|       |-- task.json       # Task metadata\n|       +-- prd.md          # Requirements doc\n|-- spec/                   # \"AI Training Data\" - project knowledge\n|   |-- frontend/           # Frontend conventions\n|   |-- backend/            # Backend conventions\n|   +-- guides/             # Thinking patterns\n+-- scripts/                # Automation tools\n```\n\n### Understanding spec/ subdirectories\n\n**frontend/** - Single-layer frontend knowledge:\n- Component patterns (how to write components in THIS project)\n- State management rules (Redux? Zustand? Context?)\n- Styling conventions (CSS modules? Tailwind? Styled-components?)\n- Hook patterns (custom hooks, data fetching)\n\n**backend/** - Single-layer backend knowledge:\n- API design patterns (REST? GraphQL? tRPC?)\n- Database conventions (query patterns, migrations)\n- Error handling standards\n- Logging and monitoring rules\n\n**guides/** - Cross-layer thinking guides:\n- Code reuse thinking guide\n- Cross-layer thinking guide\n- Pre-implementation checklists\n\n---\n\n## COMMAND DEEP DIVE\n\n### /trellis:start - Restore AI Memory\n\n**WHY IT EXISTS**:\nWhen a human engineer joins a project, they spend days/weeks learning: What is this project? What''s been built? What''s in progress? What''s the current state?\n\nAI needs the same onboarding - but compressed into seconds at session start.\n\n**WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES**:\n1. Reads developer identity (who am I in this project?)\n2. Checks git status (what branch? uncommitted changes?)\n3. Reads recent session history from `workspace/` (what happened before?)\n4. Identifies active features (what''s in progress?)\n5. Understands current project state before making any changes\n\n**WHY THIS MATTERS**:\n- Without /trellis:start: AI is blind. It might work on wrong branch, conflict with others'' work, or redo already-completed work.\n- With /trellis:start: AI knows project context, can continue where previous session left off, avoids conflicts.\n\n---\n\n### /trellis:before-frontend-dev and /trellis:before-backend-dev - Inject Specialized Knowledge\n\n**WHY IT EXISTS**:\nAI models have \"pre-trained knowledge\" - general patterns from millions of codebases. But YOUR project has specific conventions that differ from generic patterns.\n\n**WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES**:\n1. Reads `.trellis/spec/frontend/` or `.trellis/spec/backend/`\n2. Loads project-specific patterns into AI''s working context:\n   - Component naming conventions\n   - State management patterns\n   - Database query patterns\n   - Error handling standards\n\n**WHY THIS MATTERS**:\n- Without before-*-dev: AI writes generic code that doesn''t match project style.\n- With before-*-dev: AI writes code that looks like the rest of the codebase.\n\n---\n\n### /trellis:check-frontend and /trellis:check-backend - Combat Context Drift\n\n**WHY IT EXISTS**:\nAI context window has limited capacity. As conversation progresses, guidelines injected at session start become less influential. This causes \"context drift.\"\n\n**WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES**:\n1. Re-reads the guidelines that were injected earlier\n2. Compares written code against those guidelines\n3. Runs type checker and linter\n4. Identifies violations and suggests fixes\n\n**WHY THIS MATTERS**:\n- Without check-*: Context drift goes unnoticed, code quality degrades.\n- With check-*: Drift is caught and corrected before commit.\n\n---\n\n### /trellis:check-cross-layer - Multi-Dimension Verification\n\n**WHY IT EXISTS**:\nMost bugs don''t come from lack of technical skill - they come from \"didn''t think of it\":\n- Changed a constant in one place, missed 5 other places\n- Modified database schema, forgot to update the API layer\n- Created a utility function, but similar one already exists\n\n**WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES**:\n1. Identifies which dimensions your change involves\n2. For each dimension, runs targeted checks:\n   - Cross-layer data flow\n   - Code reuse analysis\n   - Import path validation\n   - Consistency checks\n\n---\n\n### /trellis:finish-work - Holistic Pre-Commit Review\n\n**WHY IT EXISTS**:\nThe `/check-*` commands focus on code quality within a single layer. But real changes often have cross-cutting concerns.\n\n**WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES**:\n1. Reviews all changes holistically\n2. Checks cross-layer consistency\n3. Identifies broader impacts\n4. Checks if new patterns should be documented\n\n---\n\n### /trellis:record-session - Persist Memory for Future\n\n**WHY IT EXISTS**:\nAll the context AI built during this session will be lost when session ends. The next session''s `/trellis:start` needs this information.\n\n**WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES**:\n1. Records session summary to `workspace/{developer}/journal-N.md`\n2. Captures what was done, learned, and what''s remaining\n3. Updates index files for quick lookup\n\n---\n\n## REAL-WORLD WORKFLOW EXAMPLES\n\n### Example 1: Bug Fix Session\n\n**[1/8] /trellis:start** - AI needs project context before touching code\n**[2/8] python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create \"Fix bug\" --slug fix-bug** - Track work for future reference\n**[3/8] /trellis:before-frontend-dev** - Inject project-specific frontend knowledge\n**[4/8] Investigate and fix the bug** - Actual development work\n**[5/8] /trellis:check-frontend** - Re-verify code against guidelines\n**[6/8] /trellis:finish-work** - Holistic cross-layer review\n**[7/8] Human tests and commits** - Human validates before code enters repo\n**[8/8] /trellis:record-session** - Persist memory for future sessions\n\n### Example 2: Planning Session (No Code)\n\n**[1/4] /trellis:start** - Context needed even for non-coding work\n**[2/4] python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create \"Planning task\" --slug planning-task** - Planning is valuable work\n**[3/4] Review docs, create subtask list** - Actual planning work\n**[4/4] /trellis:record-session (with --summary)** - Planning decisions must be recorded\n\n### Example 3: Code Review Fixes\n\n**[1/6] /trellis:start** - Resume context from previous session\n**[2/6] /trellis:before-backend-dev** - Re-inject guidelines before fixes\n**[3/6] Fix each CR issue** - Address feedback with guidelines in context\n**[4/6] /trellis:check-backend** - Verify fixes didn''t introduce new issues\n**[5/6] /trellis:finish-work** - Document lessons from CR\n**[6/6] Human commits, then /trellis:record-session** - Preserve CR lessons\n\n### Example 4: Large Refactoring\n\n**[1/5] /trellis:start** - Clear baseline before major changes\n**[2/5] Plan phases** - Break into verifiable chunks\n**[3/5] Execute phase by phase with /check-* after each** - Incremental verification\n**[4/5] /trellis:finish-work** - Check if new patterns should be documented\n**[5/5] Record with multiple commit hashes** - Link all commits to one feature\n\n### Example 5: Debug Session\n\n**[1/6] /trellis:start** - See if this bug was investigated before\n**[2/6] /trellis:before-backend-dev** - Guidelines might document known gotchas\n**[3/6] Investigation** - Actual debugging work\n**[4/6] /trellis:check-backend** - Verify debug changes don''t break other things\n**[5/6] /trellis:finish-work** - Debug findings might need documentation\n**[6/6] Human commits, then /trellis:record-session** - Debug knowledge is valuable\n\n---\n\n## KEY RULES TO EMPHASIZE\n\n1. **AI NEVER commits** - Human tests and approves. AI prepares, human validates.\n2. **Guidelines before code** - /before-*-dev commands inject project knowledge.\n3. **Check after code** - /check-* commands catch context drift.\n4. **Record everything** - /trellis:record-session persists memory.\n\n---\n\n# PART 3: Customize Your Development Guidelines\n\nAfter explaining Part 1 and Part 2, check if the project''s development guidelines need customization.\n\n## Step 1: Check Current Guidelines Status\n\nCheck if `.trellis/spec/` contains empty templates or customized guidelines:\n\n```bash\n# Check if files are still empty templates (look for placeholder text)\ngrep -l \"To be filled by the team\" .trellis/spec/backend/*.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l\ngrep -l \"To be filled by the team\" .trellis/spec/frontend/*.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l\n```\n\n## Step 2: Determine Situation\n\n**Situation A: First-time setup (empty templates)**\n\nIf guidelines are empty templates (contain \"To be filled by the team\"), this is the first time using Trellis in this project.\n\nExplain to the developer:\n\n\"I see that the development guidelines in `.trellis/spec/` are still empty templates. This is normal for a new Trellis setup!\n\nThe templates contain placeholder text that needs to be replaced with YOUR project''s actual conventions. Without this, `/before-*-dev` commands won''t provide useful guidance.\n\n**Your first task should be to fill in these guidelines:**\n\n1. Look at your existing codebase\n2. Identify the patterns and conventions already in use\n3. Document them in the guideline files\n\nFor example, for `.trellis/spec/backend/database-guidelines.md`:\n- What ORM/query library does your project use?\n- How are migrations managed?\n- What naming conventions for tables/columns?\n\nWould you like me to help you analyze your codebase and fill in these guidelines?\"\n\n**Situation B: Guidelines already customized**\n\nIf guidelines have real content (no \"To be filled\" placeholders), this is an existing setup.\n\nExplain to the developer:\n\n\"Great! Your team has already customized the development guidelines. You can start using `/before-*-dev` commands right away.\n\nI recommend reading through `.trellis/spec/` to familiarize yourself with the team''s coding standards.\"\n\n## Step 3: Help Fill Guidelines (If Empty)\n\nIf the developer wants help filling guidelines, create a feature to track this:\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create \"Fill spec guidelines\" --slug fill-spec-guidelines\n```\n\nThen systematically analyze the codebase and fill each guideline file:\n\n1. **Analyze the codebase** - Look at existing code patterns\n2. **Document conventions** - Write what you observe, not ideals\n3. **Include examples** - Reference actual files in the project\n4. **List forbidden patterns** - Document anti-patterns the team avoids\n\nWork through one file at a time:\n- `backend/directory-structure.md`\n- `backend/database-guidelines.md`\n- `backend/error-handling.md`\n- `backend/quality-guidelines.md`\n- `backend/logging-guidelines.md`\n- `frontend/directory-structure.md`\n- `frontend/component-guidelines.md`\n- `frontend/hook-guidelines.md`\n- `frontend/state-management.md`\n- `frontend/quality-guidelines.md`\n- `frontend/type-safety.md`\n\n---\n\n## Completing the Onboard Session\n\nAfter covering all three parts, summarize:\n\n\"You''re now onboarded to the Trellis workflow system! Here''s what we covered:\n- Part 1: Core concepts (why this workflow exists)\n- Part 2: Real-world examples (how to apply the workflow)\n- Part 3: Guidelines status (empty templates need filling / already customized)\n\n**Next steps** (tell user):\n1. Run `/trellis:record-session` to record this onboard session\n2. [If guidelines empty] Start filling in `.trellis/spec/` guidelines\n3. [If guidelines ready] Start your first development task\n\nWhat would you like to do first?\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:26:23.829Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code and Cursor needing comprehensive onboarding to all-in-one AI framework and toolkit","zh":"适合于需要全面入门所有在一体化AI框架和工具包的AI代理，如Claude Code和Cursor","ja":"Claude CodeやCursorのような、包括的なオンボーディングが必要なAIエージェントに適しています。すべてのオールインワンAIフレームワークとツールキット","ko":"클라우드 코드 및 커서와 같은 모든 인공 지능 프레임 워크 및 툴킷에 대한 포괄적인 온보딩이 필요한 인공 지능 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code y Cursor que necesitan una integración completa a un marco y kit de herramientas de IA todo en uno","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA comme Claude Code et Cursor nécessitant une intégration complète à un cadre et un kit d''outils d''IA tout-en-un","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und Cursor, die eine umfassende Integration in ein KI-Framework und -Toolkit benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e Cursor que necessitam de uma integração abrangente a uma estrutura e kit de ferramentas de IA all-in-one","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и Cursor, которым необходима комплексная интеграция с единой платформой и набором инструментов ИИ","ar":"مثالي لويبوتات الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و Cursor التي تحتاج إلى دمج شامل في إطار و أدوات جميع في واحد للذكاء الاصطناعي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly integrate into AI-assisted workflow systems using core concepts like command deep dives, system structure, and core philosophy, leveraging libraries and protocols for efficient collaboration","zh":"赋予代理无缝集成到AI辅助工作流系统的能力，使用诸如命令深度挖掘、系统结构和核心哲学等核心概念，利用库和协议实现高效的协作","ja":"コマンドの深い掘り下げ、システム構造、コア哲学などの基本概念を使用して、AIエージェントがAIアシストワークフローシステムにシームレスに統合できるようにし、ライブラリとプロトコルを利用して効率的なコラボレーションを実現する","ko":"명령어의 심층 분석, 시스템 구조 및 핵심 철학 등의 핵심 개념을 사용하여 인공 지능 에이전트가 인공 지능 지원 워크플로 시스템에 무缝으로 통합할 수 있도록 하며, 라이브러리 및 프로토콜을 활용하여 효율적인 협력을实现합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a integrarse sin problemas en sistemas de flujo de trabajo asistidos por IA utilizando conceptos básicos como inmersiones profundas de comandos, estructura del sistema y filosofía básica, aprovechando bibliotecas y protocolos para una colaboración eficiente","fr":"Permet aux agents de s''intégrer sans problème dans les systèmes de flux de travail assistés par l''IA en utilisant des concepts de base tels que des plongées profondes de commandes, la structure du système et la philosophie de base, en exploitant les bibliothèques et les protocoles pour une collaboration efficace","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, sich nahtlos in KI-gestützte Workflow-Systeme zu integrieren, indem sie grundlegende Konzepte wie Befehls-Deep-Dives, Systemstruktur und Kernphilosophie verwenden, um Bibliotheken und Protokolle für eine effiziente Zusammenarbeit zu nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a integrarem-se de forma transparente em sistemas de fluxo de trabalho assistidos por IA, utilizando conceitos básicos como mergulhos profundos em comandos, estrutura de sistema e filosofia básica, aproveitando bibliotecas e protocolos para colaboração eficiente","ru":"Позволяет агентам бесшовно интегрироваться в системы рабочих процессов,辅助ных ИИ, используя базовые понятия, такие как глубокие погружения в команды, структура системы и основная философия, используя библиотеки и протоколы для эффективного сотрудничества","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الاندماج بشكل عديم الجهد في أنظمة سير عمل مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي، باستخدام مفاهيم أساسية مثل الغوص العميق في أوامر، هيكل النظام والفلسفة الأساسية، واستخدام المكتبات والبروتوكولات للتعاون الفعال"},"useCases":{"en":["Onboarding new team members to AI-assisted workflow systems","Explaining underlying principles of AI commands and workflows","Mentoring developers on best practices for AI-assisted development"],"zh":["将新团队成员纳入AI辅助工作流系统的入门","解释AI命令和工作流的底层原理","指导开发人员进行AI辅助开发的最佳实践"],"ja":["AIアシストワークフローシステムへの新しいチームメンバーのオンボーディング","AIコマンドとワークフローの根底にある原理の説明","AIアシスト開発のベストプラクティスに関する開発者の指導"],"ko":["새로운 팀 구성원을 인공 지능 지원 워크플로 시스템에 온보딩하는 것","인공 지능 명령 및 워크플로의 기본 원리의 설명","인공 지능 지원 개발에 대한 개발자 교육"],"es":["Integrar nuevos miembros del equipo en sistemas de flujo de trabajo asistidos por IA","Explicar los principios subyacentes de los comandos y flujos de trabajo de IA","Asesorar a los desarrolladores sobre las mejores prácticas para el desarrollo asistido por IA"],"fr":["Intégrer de nouveaux membres d''équipe dans les systèmes de flux de travail assistés par l''IA","Expliquer les principes sous-jacents des commandes et des flux de travail d''IA","Conseiller les développeurs sur les meilleures pratiques pour le développement assisté par l''IA"],"de":["Neue Teammitglieder in KI-gestützte Workflow-Systeme integrieren","Die zugrunde liegenden Prinzipien von KI-Befehlen und -Workflows erklären","Entwickler über die besten Praktiken für die KI-gestützte Entwicklung beraten"],"pt":["Integração de novos membros da equipe em sistemas de fluxo de trabalho assistidos por IA","Explicação dos princípios subjacentes dos comandos e fluxos de trabalho de IA","Orientação de desenvolvedores sobre as melhores práticas para desenvolvimento assistido por IA"],"ru":["Интеграция новых членов команды в системы рабочих процессов,辅助ных ИИ","Объяснение основных принципов команд и рабочих процессов ИИ","Наставление разработчиков по лучшим практикам разработки,輔助ной ИИ"],"ar":["دمج أعضاء جدد في الفريق في أنظمة سير عمل مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي","شرح المبادئ الأساسية لأوامر و سير عمل الذكاء الاصطناعي","توجيه المطورين حول أفضل الممارسات لتطوير مدعوم بالذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires comprehensive content analysis","Limited to Claude Code and Cursor AI frameworks"],"zh":["需要进行全面内容分析","仅限于Claude Code和Cursor AI框架"],"ja":["包括的なコンテンツ分析が必要","Claude CodeとCursorのAIフレームワークのみに限定"],"ko":["포괄적인 콘텐츠 분석이 필요","클라우드 코드 및 커서 인공 지능 프레임 워크에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere un análisis de contenido integral","Limitado a los marcos de IA Claude Code y Cursor"],"fr":["Nécessite une analyse de contenu complète","Limité aux cadres d''IA Claude Code et Cursor"],"de":["Erfordert eine umfassende Inhaltsanalyse","Begrenzt auf die KI-Frameworks Claude Code und Cursor"],"pt":["Exige análise abrangente de conteúdo","Limitado a estruturas de IA Claude Code e Cursor"],"ru":["Требует комплексного анализа содержания","Ограничен платформами ИИ Claude Code и Cursor"],"ar":["يتطلب تحليلا شاملا للمحتوى","محدود بإطار عمل Claude Code و Cursor للذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ca110533dba054447c4e51de55af8269ad789e42704fc362cc46d03d70e69dd8","qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('mich3333/mich3333/subagents-discipline', 'community', 'mich3333', 'mich3333', 'mich3333/mich3333', 'subagents-discipline', 0, 0, 40, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.932Z', '2026-03-02T02:32:04.482Z', '8d97dd2a7e55b761fdea9cdff2cf0beac18fe41487212eca3312487eca6e54d4', '{"id":"mich3333/mich3333/subagents-discipline","name":"subagents-discipline","description":{"zh":"subagents-discipline配置文件用于管理GitHub配置，优化开发者体验","ja":"subagents-discipline構成ファイルは、GitHubの設定を管理して開発者の体験を最適化する","ko":"subagents-discipline 설정 파일은 GitHub 설정을 관리하여 개발자 경험을 최적화합니다","es":"Subagents-discipline es una herramienta de AI que proporciona archivos de configuración para perfiles de GitHub, facilitando la gestión de proyectos","fr":"Subagents-discipline est un outil d''IA qui fournit des fichiers de configuration pour les profils GitHub, facilitant la gestion des projets","de":"Subagents-discipline ist ein KI-Tool, das Konfigurationsdateien für GitHub-Profile bereitstellt, um die Projektverwaltung zu erleichtern","pt":"Configuração de subagentes para perfil GitHub utilizando ferramentas de IA de código aberto","ru":"Настройка субагентов для профиля GitHub с помощью инструментов ИИ с открытым исходным кодом","ar":"تكوين الإعدادات الفرعية لملف تعريف GitHub باستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي مفتوحة المصدر","en":"Config files for my GitHub profile."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理 субagents-discipline 配置文件","ja":"AIエージェント subagents-discipline 構成ファイル","ko":"AI 에이전트 subagents-discipline 설정 파일","es":"Herramientas de AI: subagents-discipline","fr":"Outils d''IA: subagents-discipline","de":"KI-Tools: subagents-discipline","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Subagentes Disciplina Configuração","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Настройка конфигурации Subagents-discipline","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: تكوين ملفات تعريف Subagents-disci...","en":"subagents-discipline"},"description":{"zh":"subagents-discipline配置文件用于管理GitHub配置，优化开发者体验","ja":"subagents-discipline構成ファイルは、GitHubの設定を管理して開発者の体験を最適化する","ko":"subagents-discipline 설정 파일은 GitHub 설정을 관리하여 개발자 경험을 최적화합니다","es":"Subagents-discipline es una herramienta de AI que proporciona archivos de configuración para perfiles de GitHub, facilitando la gestión de proyectos","fr":"Subagents-discipline est un outil d''IA qui fournit des fichiers de configuration pour les profils GitHub, facilitant la gestion des projets","de":"Subagents-discipline ist ein KI-Tool, das Konfigurationsdateien für GitHub-Profile bereitstellt, um die Projektverwaltung zu erleichtern","pt":"Configuração de subagentes para perfil GitHub utilizando ferramentas de IA de código aberto","ru":"Настройка субагентов для профиля GitHub с помощью инструментов ИИ с открытым исходным кодом","ar":"تكوين الإعدادات الفرعية لملف تعريف GitHub باستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي مفتوحة المصدر","en":"Config files for my GitHub profile."},"definition":{"en":"Config files for my GitHub profile."},"features":{"zh":["配置文件管理","GitHub设置优化","开发者体验提升","简单易用的配置方式","高级配置选项"],"ja":["構成ファイル管理","GitHub設定の最適化","開発者の体験の向上","シンプルで使いやすい構成方法","高度な構成オプション"],"ko":["설정 파일 관리","GitHub 설정 최적화","개발자 경험 향상","간단하고 쉬운 설정 방법","고급 설정 옵션"],"es":["Configuración de archivos para perfiles de GitHub","Gestión de proyectos con herramientas de AI","Integración con GitHub","Facilidad de uso","Personalización de configuraciones"],"fr":["Configuration de fichiers pour les profils GitHub","Gestion de projets avec des outils d''IA","Intégration avec GitHub","Facilité d''utilisation","Personnalisation des configurations"],"de":["Konfiguration von Dateien für GitHub-Profile","Projektverwaltung mit KI-Tools","Integration mit GitHub","Einfachheit der Bedienung","Anpassung von Konfigurationen"],"pt":["Configuração de subagentes para perfil GitHub","Integração com ferramentas de IA de código aberto","Personalização de configurações para necessidades específicas","Suporte a múltiplos perfis GitHub","Documentação detalhada para configuração e uso"],"ru":["Настройка субагентов для профиля GitHub","Интеграция с инструментами ИИ с открытым исходным кодом","Настройка конфигураций для конкретных потребностей","Поддержка нескольких профилей GitHub","Подробная документация для настройки и использования"],"ar":["تكوين الإعدادات الفرعية لملف تعريف GitHub","التكامل مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي مفتوحة المصدر","تخصيص الإعدادات لتلبية الاحتياجات المحددة","دعم متعددة ملفات تعريف GitHub","توثيق مفصل لتكوين واستخدام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","subagents-discipline","GitHub配置","开发者体验","配置文件管理","如何使用subagents-discipline","subagents-discipline教程","GitHub设置优化"],"ja":["AIエージェント","subagents-discipline","GitHub設定","開発者の体験","構成ファイル管理","subagents-disciplineの使い方","subagents-disciplineチュートリアル","GitHub設定の最適化"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","subagents-discipline","GitHub 설정","개발자 경험","설정 파일 관리","subagents-discipline 사용법","subagents-discipline 튜토리얼","GitHub 설정 최적화"],"es":["herramientas de AI para desarrolladores","subagents-discipline","configuración de GitHub","gestión de proyectos con AI","alternativas a subagents-discipline","cómo usar subagents-discipline","instalación de subagents-discipline","guía de configuración de subagents-discipline"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour les développeurs","subagents-discipline","configuration de GitHub","gestion de projets avec l''IA","alternatives à subagents-discipline","comment utiliser subagents-discipline","installation de subagents-discipline","guide de configuration de subagents-discipline"],"de":["KI-Tools für Entwickler","subagents-discipline","Konfiguration von GitHub","Projektverwaltung mit KI","Alternativen zu subagents-discipline","wie man subagents-discipline verwendet","Installation von subagents-discipline","Konfigurationsanleitung für subagents-discipline"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia para github","configuração de subagentes","ia para desenvolvedores","ferramentas de codigo aberto para github","como usar subagentes","subagentes vs agentes","instalação de subagentes","guia de configuração de subagentes"],"ru":["инструменты ии для github","настройка субагентов","ии для разработчиков","инструменты с открытым исходным кодом для github","как использовать субагентов","субагенты vs агенты","установка субагентов","руководство по настройке субагентов"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لجيثب","تكوين الإعدادات الفرعية","الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","أدوات مفتوحة المصدر لجيثب","كيفية استخدام الإعدادات الفرعية","الإعدادات الفرعية مقابل الوكلاء","تثبيت الإعدادات الفرعية","دليل تكوين الإعدادات الفرعية"]}},"owner":"mich3333","repo":"mich3333","repoPath":"mich3333/mich3333","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.932Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"subagents-discipline","description":"Invoke at the start of any implementation task to enforce verification-first development","bodyPreview":"# Implementation Discipline\n\n**Core principle:** Test the FEATURE, not just the component you built.\n\n---\n\n## Three Rules\n\n### Rule 1: Look Before You Code\n\nBefore writing code that touches external data (API, database, file, config):\n\n1. **Fetch/read the ACTUAL data** - run the command, see the output\n2. **Note exact field names, types, formats** - not what docs say, what you SEE\n3. **Code against what you observed** - not what you assumed\n\nThis catches: field name mismatches, wrong data shapes","body":"# Implementation Discipline\n\n**Core principle:** Test the FEATURE, not just the component you built.\n\n---\n\n## Three Rules\n\n### Rule 1: Look Before You Code\n\nBefore writing code that touches external data (API, database, file, config):\n\n1. **Fetch/read the ACTUAL data** - run the command, see the output\n2. **Note exact field names, types, formats** - not what docs say, what you SEE\n3. **Code against what you observed** - not what you assumed\n\nThis catches: field name mismatches, wrong data shapes, missing fields, format differences.\n\n```\nWITHOUT looking first:\n  Assumed: column is \"reference_images\"\n  Reality: column is \"reference_image_url\"\n  Result:  Query fails\n\nWITH looking first:\n  Ran: SELECT column_name FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = ''assets'';\n  Saw: reference_image_url\n  Coded against: reference_image_url\n  Result: Works\n```\n\n### Rule 2: Test Both Levels\n\n**Component test** catches: logic bugs, edge cases, type errors\n**Feature test** catches: integration bugs, auth issues, data flow problems\n\nBoth are required. Component test alone is NOT sufficient.\n\n| You built | Component test | Feature test |\n|-----------|----------------|--------------|\n| API endpoint | curl returns 200 | UI calls API, displays result |\n| Database change | Migration runs | App reads/writes correctly |\n| Frontend component | Renders, no errors | User can see and interact |\n| Full-stack feature | Each piece works alone | End-to-end flow works |\n\n**The pattern:**\n1. Build the thing\n2. Component test - verify your piece works in isolation\n3. Feature test - verify the integrated feature works end-to-end\n4. Only then claim done\n\n### Rule 3: Use Your Tools\n\nBefore claiming you can''t fully test:\n\n1. **Check what MCP servers you have access to** - list available tools\n2. **If any tool can help verify the feature works**, use it\n3. **Be resourceful** - browser automation, database inspection, API testing tools\n\n\"I couldn''t test the feature\" is only valid after exhausting available options.\n\n---\n\n## DEMO Block (Required)\n\nEvery completion must include evidence. Code reviewer will verify this.\n\n```\nDEMO:\n  COMPONENT:\n    Command: [what you ran to test the component]\n    Result: [what you observed]\n\n  FEATURE:\n    Steps: [how you tested the integrated feature]\n    Result: [what you observed - screenshot, output, etc.]\n```\n\n### When Full Feature Test Isn''t Possible\n\nIf you genuinely cannot test end-to-end (long-running job, external service, no browser tools):\n\n```\nDEMO:\n  COMPONENT:\n    Command: curl localhost:3008/api/endpoint\n    Result: 200, returns expected data\n\n  FEATURE: PARTIAL\n    Verified: [what you could test]\n    Needs human check: [what still needs verification]\n    Why: [specific reason - no browser MCP, takes 10+ minutes, requires external service]\n```\n\n**Not acceptable reasons for PARTIAL:**\n- \"Server wasn''t running\" → start it\n- \"Didn''t have test data\" → create it\n- \"Would take too long\" → if < 2 minutes, do it\n\n**Acceptable reasons:**\n- No browser/UI automation tools available\n- External API with rate limits or costs\n- Job takes > 5 minutes to complete\n- Requires production data that can''t be mocked\n\n---\n\n## For Epic Children\n\nIf your BEAD_ID contains a dot (e.g., BD-001.2), you''re implementing part of a larger feature:\n\n1. **Check for design doc**: `bd show {EPIC_ID} --json | jq -r ''.[0].design''`\n2. **Read it if it exists** - this is your contract\n3. **Match it exactly** - same field names, same types, same shapes\n\nDesign docs ensure all pieces fit together. If you deviate, integration fails.\n\n---\n\n## Completion Checklist\n\nBefore marking done:\n\n- [ ] Looked at actual data/interfaces before coding (not assumed)\n- [ ] Component test passes (your piece works in isolation)\n- [ ] Feature test passes OR documented as PARTIAL with valid reason\n- [ ] DEMO block included with evidence\n- [ ] Used available tools to test (checked MCP servers, used what helps)\n\n---\n\n## Red Flags - Stop and Verify\n\nWhen you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"This should work...\" → run it and see\n- \"I assume the field is...\" → look at the actual data\n- \"I''ll test it later...\" → test it now\n- \"It''s too simple to break...\" → verify anyway\n\nWhen you''re about to say:\n- \"Done!\" / \"Fixed!\" / \"Should work now!\" → show the DEMO first\n\n---\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n```\nComponent test passing ≠ feature works\nCurl returning 200 ≠ UI displays correctly\nTypeScript compiles ≠ user can use it\n```\n\nTest the feature like a user would use it. Then show evidence. Then claim done.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:32:04.482Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing rigorous testing and validation of external data interactions, such as those involving APIs, databases, or config files.","zh":"非常适合需要对外部数据交互进行严格测试和验证的AI代理，例如涉及API、数据库或配置文件的交互。","ja":"外部データのインタラクションを徹底的にテストおよび検証する必要があるAIエージェントに最適です。たとえば、API、データベース、またはコンフィグファイルを含むものです。","ko":"외부 데이터 상호 작용에 대한 엄격한 테스트 및 검증이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어, API, 데이터베이스 또는 구성 파일과 같은 상호 작용이 있습니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA que necesitan pruebas y validación rigurosas de interacciones de datos externos, como aquellas que involucran APIs, bases de datos o archivos de configuración.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents IA nécessitant des tests et une validation rigoureux des interactions de données externes, comme celles impliquant des APIs, des bases de données ou des fichiers de configuration.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die strenge Tests und Validierungen von externen Dateninteraktionen benötigen, wie z.B. solche, die APIs, Datenbanken oder Konfigurationsdateien umfassen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de testes e validação rigorosos de interações de dados externos, como aqueles que envolvem APIs, bancos de dados ou arquivos de configuração.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, требующих тщательного тестирования и проверки взаимодействий с внешними данными, такими как те, которые включают API, базы данных или файлы конфигурации.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى اختبارات وتحقق صارم للتفاعلات البيانية الخارجية، مثل تلك التي تتضمن واجهات برمجة التطبيقات أو قواعد البيانات أو ملفات التكوين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write robust code by fetching and analyzing actual data, noting exact field names and types, and coding against observed data shapes and formats, using protocols and file formats like config files and APIs.","zh":"通过获取和分析实际数据、记录确切的字段名称和类型以及针对观察到的数据形状和格式进行编码，使用诸如配置文件和API的协议和文件格式，使代理能够编写强大的代码。","ja":"実際のデータを取得して分析し、正確なフィールド名とタイプを記録し、観測されたデータの形状と形式に対してコード化し、コンフィグファイルやAPIなどのプロトコルとファイル形式を使用することで、エージェントが堅牢なコードを書くことを可能にします。","ko":"실제 데이터를 가져와 분석하고 정확한 필드 이름과 유형을 기록하고 관찰된 데이터의 모양과 형식에 대해 코딩하고 구성 파일 및 API와 같은 프로토콜 및 파일 형식을 사용하여 에이전트가 강력한 코드를 작성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir código robusto al recuperar y analizar datos reales, anotar nombres y tipos de campo exactos y codificar contra formas y formatos de datos observados, utilizando protocolos y formatos de archivo como archivos de configuración y APIs.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire un code robuste en récupérant et en analysant des données réelles, en notant les noms et les types de champ exacts et en codant contre les formes et les formats de données observés, en utilisant des protocoles et des formats de fichier tels que des fichiers de configuration et des APIs.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, robusten Code zu schreiben, indem sie reale Daten abrufen und analysieren, genaue Feldnamen und -typen notieren und gegen beobachtete Datenformen und -formate codieren, unter Verwendung von Protokollen und Dateiformaten wie Konfigurationsdateien und APIs.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escreverem código robusto ao buscar e analisar dados reais, observando nomes de campos exatos e tipos, e codificando contra formas e formatos de dados observados, usando protocolos e formatos de arquivo como arquivos de configuração e APIs.","ru":"Позволяет агентам писать прочный код, получая и анализируя фактические данные, отмечая точные имена полей и типы, и кодируя против наблюдаемых форм и форматов данных, используя протоколы и форматы файлов, такие как файлы конфигурации и API.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على كتابة رمز متين من خلال استرجاع وتحليل البيانات الفعلية، وملاحظة أسماء الحقول بالضبط وأنواعها، والترميز ضد أشكال وتنسيقات البيانات المحسنة، باستخدام بروتوكولات وتنسيقات الملفات مثل ملفات التكوين وواجهات برمجة التطبيقات."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging field name mismatches and data shape inconsistencies","Validating assumptions about external data before coding","Implementing the ''Look Before You Code'' discipline for reliable data interactions"],"zh":["调试字段名称不匹配和数据形状不一致","在编码前验证外部数据的假设","实施''查看后编码''的学科以进行可靠的数据交互"],"ja":["フィールド名の不一致とデータの形状の不一致をデバッグする","コード化する前に外部データに関する仮定を検証する","信頼性の高いデータのやり取りのために''コード化する前に確認する''の学問を実施する"],"ko":["필드 이름 불일치 및 데이터 모양 불일치를 디버깅하는 것","코딩하기 전에 외부 데이터에 대한 가정을 검증하는 것","안정적인 데이터 상호 작용을 위해 ''코딩하기 전에 확인하기''의 학문을 구현하는 것"],"es":["Depuración de errores de nombres de campo y inconsistencias de forma de datos","Validación de suposiciones sobre datos externos antes de la codificación","Implementación de la disciplina ''Mira antes de codificar'' para interacciones de datos confiables"],"fr":["Débogage des erreurs de noms de champ et des incohérences de forme de données","Validation des hypothèses sur les données externes avant la codification","Mise en œuvre de la discipline ''Regarde avant de coder'' pour des interactions de données fiables"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei Feldnamenfehlern und Datenforminkonsistenzen","Validierung von Annahmen über externe Daten vor der Codierung","Implementierung der Disziplin ''Sieh vor dem Codieren'' für zuverlässige Dateninteraktionen"],"pt":["Depurar discrepâncias de nomes de campos e inconsistências de forma de dados","Validar suposições sobre dados externos antes de codificar","Implementar a disciplina ''Olhe Antes de Codificar'' para interações de dados confiáveis"],"ru":["Отладка несоответствий имен полей и несоответствий форм данных","Проверка предположений о внешних данных перед кодированием","Реализация дисциплины ''Смотрите перед кодированием'' для надежных взаимодействий с данными"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء عدم مطابقة أسماء الحقول وعدم تطابق أشكال البيانات","التحقق من افتراضات حول البيانات الخارجية قبل الترميز","تنفيذ منهج ''انظر قبل الترميز'' للتفاعلات البيانية الموثوقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to external data sources like APIs or databases","Needs ability to run commands and observe output for data validation"],"zh":["需要访问外部数据源，如API或数据库","需要运行命令和观察输出以进行数据验证"],"ja":["APIまたはデータベースなどの外部データソースへのアクセスが必要","データの検証のためにコマンドを実行し、出力を観察する能力が必要"],"ko":["API 또는 데이터베이스와 같은 외부 데이터 소스에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","데이터를 검증하기 위해 명령을 실행하고 출력을 관찰하는 기능이 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a fuentes de datos externas como APIs o bases de datos","Necesita la capacidad de ejecutar comandos y observar la salida para la validación de datos"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à des sources de données externes comme des APIs ou des bases de données","A besoin de la capacité d''exécuter des commandes et d''observer la sortie pour la validation des données"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf externe Datenquellen wie APIs oder Datenbanken","Benötigt die Fähigkeit, Befehle auszuführen und die Ausgabe für die Datavalidierung zu beobachten"],"pt":["Requer acesso a fontes de dados externas como APIs ou bancos de dados","Necessita capacidade de executar comandos e observar saída para validação de dados"],"ru":["Требует доступа к внешним источникам данных, таким как API или базы данных","Требует возможности запускать команды и наблюдать вывод для проверки данных"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مصادر بيانات خارجية مثل واجهات برمجة التطبيقات أو قواعد البيانات","يتطلب القدرة على تشغيل الأوامرและมلاحظة الإخراج للتحقق من البيانات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"8d97dd2a7e55b761fdea9cdff2cf0beac18fe41487212eca3312487eca6e54d4","qualityScore":40}');
