requisitos","Análise de necessidades","Documentação de requisitos","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Suporte a linguagens de programação como Python e Node.js"],"ru":["Идентификация требований","Анализ потребностей","Документирование требований","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Поддержка языков программирования seperti Python и Node.js"],"ar":["تحديد المتطلبات","تحليل الاحتياجات","توثيق المتطلبات","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل Python و Node.js"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","需求分析工具","如何使用AI智能代理","什么是需求分析","AI智能代理替代品","需求分析工具安装指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","要件分析ツール","AIエージェントの使用方法","要件分析とは","AIエージェントの代替品","要件分析ツールの設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","요구사항 분석 도구","AI 에이전트 사용법","요구사항 분석이란","AI 에이전트 대체품","요구사항 분석 도구 설치 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar herramientas de inteligencia artificial","qué es el análisis de requisitos","herramientas de inteligencia artificial para YouTube","alternativas a las herramientas de análisis de requisitos","instalación de herramientas de inteligencia artificial","guía de configuración para herramientas de inteligencia artificial","análisis de requisitos vs análisis de datos","herramientas de inteligencia artificial para desarrolladores"],"fr":["comment utiliser les outils d''intelligence artificielle","quoi est l''analyse de besoins","outils d''intelligence artificielle pour YouTube","alternatives aux outils d''analyse de besoins","installation d''outils d''intelligence artificielle","guide de configuration pour les outils d''intelligence artificielle","analyse de besoins vs analyse de données","outils d''intelligence artificielle pour les développeurs"],"de":["wie man KI-Tools verwendet","was ist die Anforderungsanalyse","KI-Tools für YouTube","Alternativen zu Anforderungsanalyse-Tools","Installation von KI-Tools","Konfigurationsanleitung für KI-Tools","Anforderungsanalyse vs Datenanalyse","KI-Tools für Entwickler"],"pt":["análise de requisitos","ferramentas de IA","desenvolvimento de software","requisitos de projeto","como usar ferramentas de IA","o que é análise de requisitos","alternativas para análise de requisitos","instalação de ferramentas de IA","guia de configuração de ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","анализ требований","разработка программного обеспечения","требования проекта","как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое анализ требований","альтернативы для анализа требований","установка ИИ Агентов","руководство по настройке ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحليل المتطلبات","تطوير البرمجيات","متطلبات المشروع","كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو تحليل المتطلبات","بديلات لتحليل المتطلبات","تثبيت أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","دليل إعداد أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"aizhimou","repo":"pigeon-pod","repoPath":"aizhimou/pigeon-pod","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.968Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"requirements-analysis","description":"Analyze product/feature requirements for the PigeonPod project with software engineering rigor. Use when users ask to evaluate a requirements value, feasibility, architecture fit, implementation impact, risk, delivery scope, or tradeoffs. Always inspect current repository docs/code first (especially architecture and README files), then use MCP tools (including Context7) to verify external library/framework/API constraints before concluding.","bodyPreview":"# Requirements Analysis\n\nAnalyze requirements against PigeonPod goals, current architecture, and implementation reality.\n\n## Follow This Workflow\n\n1. Restate the requirement in one short paragraph.\n2. Identify requirement type: `feature`, `enhancement`, `bugfix`, `non-functional`, `integration`, or `migration`.\n3. Define expected user value and business value.\n4. Read relevant project docs and code before giving conclusions.\n5. Use MCP/Context7 to confirm dependency or API constraints when exter","body":"# Requirements Analysis\n\nAnalyze requirements against PigeonPod goals, current architecture, and implementation reality.\n\n## Follow This Workflow\n\n1. Restate the requirement in one short paragraph.\n2. Identify requirement type: `feature`, `enhancement`, `bugfix`, `non-functional`, `integration`, or `migration`.\n3. Define expected user value and business value.\n4. Read relevant project docs and code before giving conclusions.\n5. Use MCP/Context7 to confirm dependency or API constraints when external libraries/services are involved.\n6. Evaluate architecture fit, implementation complexity, data impact, and operational impact.\n7. Propose an implementation strategy with phased scope (`MVP`, `next`, `later`).\n8. Output a decision with explicit rationale and open questions.\n\n## Read Local Context First\n\nPrioritize these files for PigeonPod:\n\n- `README.md`\n- `dev-docs/architecture/architecture-design-en.md`\n- `backend/src/main/resources/application.yml`\n- `backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/*.sql`\n- Relevant backend packages under `backend/src/main/java/top/asimov/pigeon/`\n- Relevant frontend routes/components under `frontend/src/pages/` and `frontend/src/components/`\n\nUse fast discovery commands when needed:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"keyword|concept|module\" backend/src/main/java frontend/src dev-docs README.md\nrg --files dev-docs/\n```\n\n## Use Context7 and MCP Deliberately\n\nUse Context7/MCP when the requirement depends on framework/library/service behavior, version constraints, configuration, or integration details.\n\nTypical triggers:\n\n- Spring Boot/MyBatis-Plus/Sa-Token behavior or config decisions\n- React/Mantine/React Router/i18next/Axios constraints\n- YouTube Data API v3 limits/quotas/contract details\n- RSS/Podcasting namespace compatibility details\n- yt-dlp options/behavior and compatibility implications\n\nRules:\n\n- Resolve library ID first, then query focused questions.\n- Prefer primary/official docs and version-aware guidance.\n- Distinguish facts from inference.\n- If docs conflict with local implementation, prioritize local code reality and call out the gap.\n\n## Evaluate With These Dimensions\n\nAssess each dimension explicitly:\n\n1. Value Alignment: Match with PigeonPod core goals (YouTube-to-podcast conversion, auto-sync/download, feed usability, operations simplicity).\n2. Feasibility: Confirm technical possibility with current stack and constraints.\n3. Architecture Fit: Check compatibility with backend service boundaries, scheduler/event flow, DB schema, and frontend route/state model.\n4. Data and Migration Impact: Identify new fields/tables, migration requirements, backfill, and backward compatibility.\n5. API and Contract Impact: Identify REST/RSS contract changes and consumer compatibility risks.\n6. Security and Compliance: Review auth, permissions, secrets/API keys, abuse vectors.\n7. Performance and Cost: Estimate queue pressure, I/O/download load, external API quota consumption, and storage growth.\n8. Testability and Operability: Define unit/integration/e2e coverage and monitoring/logging needs.\n\n## Produce This Output Format\n\nUse this structure in final analysis:\n\n```markdown\n## Requirement Summary\n- User request:\n- Requirement type:\n- Assumptions:\n\n## Value Assessment\n- User value:\n- Product/business value:\n- Priority suggestion: High/Medium/Low\n\n## Feasibility and Architecture Fit\n- Current touchpoints:\n- Proposed changes:\n- Architecture fit verdict: Good/Partial/Poor\n\n## Impact Analysis\n- Backend impact:\n- Frontend impact:\n- Database/migration impact:\n- External dependency impact:\n- Security/performance/ops impact:\n\n## Delivery Plan\n- MVP scope:\n- Non-MVP scope:\n- Estimated complexity: S/M/L/XL\n- Key risks and mitigations:\n\n## Decision\n- Recommendation: Proceed / Proceed with constraints / Defer / Reject\n- Reasoning:\n- Open questions:\n```\n\n## Decision Heuristics\n\n- Recommend `Proceed` when value is clear, fit is good, and risk is manageable.\n- Recommend `Proceed with constraints` when value is high but scope/risk needs staged delivery.\n- Recommend `Defer` when value exists but prerequisites are missing.\n- Recommend `Reject` when requirement conflicts with core goals or creates disproportional cost/risk.\n\n## Quality Bar\n\nBefore finalizing, verify all checks:\n\n- Base conclusions on repository evidence, not assumptions only.\n- Confirm external-library/API claims through Context7/MCP when relevant.\n- Separate facts, assumptions, and unknowns.\n- Include at least one feasible implementation path.\n- Include explicit tradeoffs and rollback/fallback considerations.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:53:09.915Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring advanced requirements analysis capabilities to align with project goals and architecture.","zh":"适用于Claude Code和AutoGPT等AI代理，需要高级需求分析能力以符合项目目标和架构。","ja":"Claude CodeやAutoGPTのようなAIエージェントに適しています。プロジェクトの目標やアーキテクチャと一致するために、高度な要件分析機能が必要です。","ko":"Claude Code와 AutoGPT 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 프로젝트 목표와 아키텍처에 맞추기 위해 고급 요구 사항 분석 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren capacidades avanzadas de análisis de requisitos para alinearlos con los objetivos y la arquitectura del proyecto.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des capacités avancées d''analyse des exigences pour les aligner sur les objectifs et l''architecture du projet.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die erweiterte Anforderungsanalysefunktionen benötigen, um sie mit den Projektzielen und der Architektur abzustimmen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e AutoGPT que requerem capacidades avançadas de análise de requisitos para alinhar com os objetivos e arquitetura do projeto.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих продвинутых возможностей анализа требований для соответствия целям и архитектуре проекта.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكيين مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يتطلبون khảائات متقدمة لتحليل المتطلبات للتطابق مع أهداف ومعمارية المشروع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to evaluate requirements against project objectives, identify requirement types such as feature, enhancement, and bugfix, and define expected user and business value using MCP/Context7 for dependency confirmation.","zh":"赋予代理评估需求与项目目标的一致性，识别需求类型（如功能、增强和bug修复），并使用MCP/Context7定义预期用户和业务价值以确认依赖关系。","ja":"エージェントが要件をプロジェクトの目的と照合し、機能、強化、バグ修正などの要件タイプを識別し、MCP/Context7を使用して期待されるユーザーとビジネス価値を定義する依存関係の確認を行うことができます。","ko":"에이전트가 요구 사항을 프로젝트 목표와 일치시키고, 기능, 향상, 버그 수정 등의 요구 사항 유형을 식별하며, MCP/Context7를 사용하여 예상 사용자 및 비즈니스 가치를 정의하여 의존성을 확인할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes evaluar los requisitos frente a los objetivos del proyecto, identificar tipos de requisitos como características, mejoras y correcciones de errores, y definir el valor esperado para el usuario y el negocio utilizando MCP/Context7 para la confirmación de dependencias.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''évaluer les exigences par rapport aux objectifs du projet, d''identifier les types d''exigences tels que les fonctionnalités, les améliorations et les corrections de bogues, et de définir la valeur attendue pour l''utilisateur et l''entreprise en utilisant MCP/Context7 pour la confirmation des dépendances.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Anforderungen im Vergleich zu den Projektzielen zu bewerten, Anforderungstypen wie Funktionen, Verbesserungen und Fehlerbehebungen zu identifizieren und den erwarteten Nutzen für den Benutzer und das Unternehmen unter Verwendung von MCP/Context7 für die Bestätigung von Abhängigkeiten zu definieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a avaliar os requisitos contra os objetivos do projeto, identificar tipos de requisitos, como recurso, melhoria e correção de bugs, e definir o valor esperado do usuário e do negócio usando MCP/Context7 para confirmação de dependência.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью оценивать требования в соответствии с целями проекта, определять типы требований, такие как функция, улучшение и исправление ошибок, и определять ожидаемую ценность пользователя и бизнеса с использованием MCP/Context7 для подтверждения зависимости.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تقييم المتطلبات مقابل أهداف المشروع، وتحديد أنواع المتطلبات مثل الميزة و التحسين وإصلاح العيوب، وتحديد القيمة المتوقعة للمستخدم والأعمال باستخدام MCP/Context7 للتأكيد على الارتباط."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing requirements for integration and migration projects","Evaluating feature requests for alignment with business objectives","Identifying non-functional requirements for system optimization"],"zh":["集成和迁移项目的需求分析","评估功能请求与业务目标的一致性","识别系统优化的非功能需求"],"ja":["統合と移行プロジェクトの要件分析","ビジネス目標との整合性を評価する機能リクエスト","システム最適化の非機能要件の特定"],"ko":["통합 및 마이그레이션 프로젝트의 요구 사항 분석","비즈니스 목표와 일치하는 기능 요청 평가","시스템 최적화를 위한 비기능적 요구 사항 식별"],"es":["Análisis de requisitos para proyectos de integración y migración","Evaluación de solicitudes de características para alinearlas con los objetivos empresariales","Identificación de requisitos no funcionales para la optimización del sistema"],"fr":["Analyse des exigences pour les projets d''intégration et de migration","Évaluation des demandes de fonctionnalités pour les aligner sur les objectifs commerciaux","Identification des exigences non fonctionnelles pour l''optimisation du système"],"de":["Analyse von Anforderungen für Integrations- und Migrationsprojekte","Bewertung von Funktionsanforderungen zur Ausrichtung an Geschäftszielen","Identifizierung von nichtfunktionalen Anforderungen zur Systemoptimierung"],"pt":["Analisar requisitos para projetos de integração e migração","Avaliar solicitações de recursos para alinhar com os objetivos comerciais","Identificar requisitos não funcionais para otimização do sistema"],"ru":["Анализ требований для проектов интеграции и миграции","Оценка запросов на функции для соответствия бизнес-целям","Определение нефункциональных требований для оптимизации системы"],"ar":["تحليل المتطلبات لمشاريع التكامل والهجرة","تقييم طلبات الميزات لتتوافق مع أهداف الأعمال","تحديد المتطلبات الغير وظيفية لتحسين النظام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to project documentation and codebase","Dependent on MCP/Context7 for constraint validation","Limited to analysis, does not include implementation"],"zh":["需要访问项目文档和代码库","依赖MCP/Context7进行约束验证","仅限分析，不包括实现"],"ja":["プロジェクトのドキュメントとコードベースへのアクセスが必要","MCP/Context7に依存して制約を検証","分析のみ、実装は含まない"],"ko":["프로젝트 문서와 코드베이스에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","MCP/Context7에 의존하여 제약을 검증합니다.","분석만 포함되며, 구현은 포함되지 않습니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a la documentación y base de código del proyecto","Depende de MCP/Context7 para la validación de restricciones","Limitado al análisis, no incluye la implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la documentation et à la base de code du projet","Dépend de MCP/Context7 pour la validation des contraintes","Limité à l''analyse, n''inclut pas la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Projektdokumentation und den Codebestand","Hängt von MCP/Context7 für die Validierung von Einschränkungen ab","Begrenzt auf die Analyse, enthält keine Implementierung"],"pt":["Requer acesso à documentação do projeto e código-fonte","Depende de MCP/Context7 para validação de restrições","Limitado à análise, não inclui implementação"],"ru":["Требует доступа к документации проекта и кодовой базе","Зависит от MCP/Context7 для проверки ограничений","Ограничен анализом, не включает реализацию"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى توثيق المشروع وقاعدة الشفرة","يعتمد على MCP/Context7 للتأكيد على القيود","محدود بالتحليل، ولا يتضمن التنفيذ"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"b73f74282df21ce869477991d072a637711dfc98cc2775d1f59372486c4a8d04","qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('mikemaccana/solana-anchor-claude-skill/solana-anchor-claude-skill', 'community', 'mikemaccana', 'solana-anchor-claude-skill', 'mikemaccana/solana-anchor-claude-skill', 'solana-anchor-claude-skill', 0, 0, 40, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.976Z', '2026-03-02T02:55:16.673Z', '3c1b635ef5d502ae56aa36c369b91d3ad5bec3790194d89fd7059685966403cf', '{"id":"mikemaccana/solana-anchor-claude-skill/solana-anchor-claude-skill","name":"solana-anchor-claude-skill","description":{"zh":"Solana Anchor Claude AI工具是用于构建高性能区块链应用的强大工具","ja":"SolanaとAnchorのClaude AIエージェントは、高性能のブロックチェーンアプリケーションを構築するための強力なツールです","ko":"솔라나 앵커 클라우드 AI 에이전트는 고성능 블록체인 애플리케이션을 구축하는 강력한 도구입니다","es":"Solana y Anchor Claude ofrecen una integración de herramientas de AI para mejorar el desarrollo de aplicaciones","fr":"Solana et Anchor Claude proposent une intégration d''outils d''IA pour améliorer le développement d''applications","de":"Solana und Anchor Claude bieten eine Integration von KI-Tools, um die Entwicklung von Anwendungen zu verbessern","pt":"A habilidade Solana e Anchor Claude é uma ferramenta poderosa para desenvolvedores de aplicações descentralizadas. Ela fornece recursos avançados para a criação de contratos inteligentes e aplicativos na blockchain Solana.","ru":"Навык Solana и Anchor Claude является мощным инструментом для разработчиков децентрализованных приложений. Он предоставляет расширенные возможности для создания умных контрактов и приложений в блокчейне Solana.","ar":"مهارة Solana و Anchor Claude هي أداة قوية للمطورين التطبيقات اللامركزية. توفر ميزات متقدمة لإنشاء عقود ذكية وتطبيقات على سلاسل الكتل Solana.","en":"The Solana and Anchor Claude skill"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Solana Anchor Claude AI工具","ja":"SolanaとAnchorのClaude AIエージェント","ko":"솔라나 앵커 클라우드 AI 에이전트","es":"Herramientas de AI: Solana y Anchor Claude","fr":"Outils d''IA: Solana et Anchor Claude","de":"KI-Tools: Solana und Anchor Claude","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Solana e Anchor Claude","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Solana и Anchor Claude","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: Solana و Anchor Claude","en":"solana-anchor-claude-skill"},"description":{"zh":"Solana Anchor Claude AI工具是用于构建高性能区块链应用的强大工具","ja":"SolanaとAnchorのClaude AIエージェントは、高性能のブロックチェーンアプリケーションを構築するための強力なツールです","ko":"솔라나 앵커 클라우드 AI 에이전트는 고성능 블록체인 애플리케이션을 구축하는 강력한 도구입니다","es":"Solana y Anchor Claude ofrecen una integración de herramientas de AI para mejorar el desarrollo de aplicaciones","fr":"Solana et Anchor Claude proposent une intégration d''outils d''IA pour améliorer le développement d''applications","de":"Solana und Anchor Claude bieten eine Integration von KI-Tools, um die Entwicklung von Anwendungen zu verbessern","pt":"A habilidade Solana e Anchor Claude é uma ferramenta poderosa para desenvolvedores de aplicações descentralizadas. Ela fornece recursos avançados para a cria...","ru":"Навык Solana и Anchor Claude является мощным инструментом для разработчиков децентрализованных приложений. Он предоставляет расширенные возможности для созда...","ar":"مهارة Solana و Anchor Claude هي أداة قوية للمطورين التطبيقات اللامركزية. توفر ميزات متقدمة لإنشاء عقود ذكية وتطبيقات على سلاسل الكتل Solana.","en":"The Solana and Anchor Claude skill"},"definition":{"en":"The Solana and Anchor Claude skill"},"features":{"zh":["支持Solana和Anchor的区块链应用构建","提供高性能的智能合约执行","支持多种编程语言，包括Python和Node.js","提供简单易用的CLI接口","支持多种AI模型和算法"],"ja":["SolanaとAnchorのブロックチェーンアプリケーション構築をサポート","高性能のスマートコントラクト実行を提供","複数のプログラミング言語、包括PythonとNode.jsをサポート","シンプルで使いやすいCLIインターフェースを提供","複数のAIモデルとアルゴリズムをサポート"],"ko":["솔라나와 앵커의 블록체인 애플리케이션 구축을 지원","고성능의 스마트 계약 실행을 제공","다양한 프로그래밍 언어, 포함 Python과 Node.js를 지원","간단하고 사용하기 쉬운 CLI 인터페이스를 제공","다양한 AI 모델과 알고리즘을 지원"],"es":["Integración de Solana y Anchor Claude","Desarrollo de aplicaciones con herramientas de AI","Mejora de la eficiencia con tecnologías de vanguardia","Soporte para desarrollo de blockchain","Implementación de inteligencia artificial en aplicaciones","Integración con CLI para desarrollo avanzado"],"fr":["Intégration de Solana et Anchor Claude","Développement d''applications avec des outils d''IA","Amélioration de l''efficacité avec des technologies de pointe","Support pour le développement de blockchain","Mise en œuvre de l''intelligence artificielle dans les applications","Intégration avec CLI pour le développement avancé"],"de":["Integration von Solana und Anchor Claude","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit KI-Tools","Verbesserung der Effizienz mit SpitzenTechnologien","Unterstützung für die Entwicklung von Blockchain","Implementierung von künstlicher Intelligenz in Anwendungen","Integration mit CLI für erweitertes Entwicklung"],"pt":["Criação de contratos inteligentes na blockchain Solana","Desenvolvimento de aplicações descentralizadas com Anchor","Integração com a rede Solana","Suporte a linguagens de programação como Rust e C++","Recursos avançados de segurança e escalabilidade"],"ru":["Создание умных контрактов в блокчейне Solana","Разработка децентрализованных приложений с Anchor","Интеграция с сетью Solana","Поддержка языков программирования như Rust и C++","Расширенные возможности безопасности и масштабируемости"],"ar":["إنشاء عقود ذكية على سلاسل الكتل Solana","تطوير التطبيقات اللامركزية مع Anchor","التكامل مع شبكة Solana","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل Rust و C++","ميزات متقدمة للأمان والتماسك"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Solana Anchor Claude AI工具","区块链应用构建","智能合约执行","Python和Node.js","CLI接口","AI模型和算法","如何使用Solana Anchor Claude AI工具","Solana Anchor Claude AI工具安装指南"],"ja":["SolanaとAnchorのClaude AIエージェント","ブロックチェーンアプリケーション構築","スマートコントラクト実行","PythonとNode.js","CLIインターフェース","AIモデルとアルゴリズム","SolanaとAnchorのClaude AIエージェントを使用する方法","SolanaとAnchorのClaude AIエージェントの設定ガイド"],"ko":["솔라나 앵커 클라우드 AI 에이전트","블록체인 애플리케이션 구축","스마트 계약 실행","Python과 Node.js","CLI 인터페이스","AI 모델과 알고리즘","솔라나 앵커 클라우드 AI 에이전트를 사용하는 방법","솔라나 앵커 클라우드 AI 에이전트의 설치 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de AI para desarrollo","Solana y Anchor Claude","desarrollo de aplicaciones con AI","guias de instalación de Solana","alternativas a Anchor Claude","Solana vs Anchor Claude","cómo usar Solana y Anchor Claude","mejores prácticas para desarrollo de blockchain","inteligencia artificial en aplicaciones","CLI para desarrollo avanzado"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour le développement","Solana et Anchor Claude","développement d''applications avec IA","guides d''installation de Solana","alternatives à Anchor Claude","Solana vs Anchor Claude","comment utiliser Solana et Anchor Claude","meilleures pratiques pour le développement de blockchain","intelligence artificielle dans les applications","CLI pour le développement avancé"],"de":["KI-Tools für die Entwicklung","Solana und Anchor Claude","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit KI","Installationsanleitungen für Solana","Alternativen zu Anchor Claude","Solana vs Anchor Claude","wie man Solana und Anchor Claude verwendet","beste Praktiken für die Entwicklung von Blockchain","künstliche Intelligenz in Anwendungen","CLI für erweitertes Entwicklung"],"pt":["como usar Solana e Anchor","o que é Solana e Anchor","desenvolvimento de aplicações descentralizadas","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","Solana vs Ethereum","instalação do Solana","guia de configuração do Anchor"],"ru":["как использовать Solana и Anchor","что такое Solana и Anchor","разработка децентрализованных приложений","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","Solana vs Ethereum","установка Solana","руководство по настройке Anchor"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Solana و Anchor","ما هي Solana و Anchor","تطوير التطبيقات اللامركزية","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","Solana مقابل Ethereum","تثبيت Solana","دليل إعداد Anchor"]}},"owner":"mikemaccana","repo":"solana-anchor-claude-skill","repoPath":"mikemaccana/solana-anchor-claude-skill","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.976Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"solana-anchor-claude-skill","description":"Use when working on Solana Anchor programs, including Rust program files, TypeScript tests, and Anchor.toml configuration. Designed to create minimal, reusable code without unecessary duplication.","bodyPreview":"# Coding Guidelines\n\nApply these rules to ensure code quality, maintainability, and adherence to project standards.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Before declaring success or celebrating, run `npm test`. If the tests fail, there is more work to do. Don''t stop until `npm test` passes on the code you have made.\n\n**CRITICAL: Placeholder tests don''t count as success.**\n- Tests that just do `assert.ok(true)` or similar are NOT real tests\n- DO NOT mark \"Write tests\" as complete until tests actually call the","body":"# Coding Guidelines\n\nApply these rules to ensure code quality, maintainability, and adherence to project standards.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- Before declaring success or celebrating, run `npm test`. If the tests fail, there is more work to do. Don''t stop until `npm test` passes on the code you have made.\n\n**CRITICAL: Placeholder tests don''t count as success.**\n- Tests that just do `assert.ok(true)` or similar are NOT real tests\n- DO NOT mark \"Write tests\" as complete until tests actually call the program instructions\n- DO NOT ask \"should I write real tests now?\" - if the tests are placeholders, write real ones immediately\n- Real tests must: initialize accounts, send transactions, verify state changes, check balances\n- If you find yourself writing placeholder tests, stop and write real integration tests instead\n\n- When summarizing your work, show the work items you have achieved with this symbol ''✅'' and there is more work to do, add a ''❌'' for each remaining work item.\n\n## Documentation Sources\n\nUse these official documentation sources:\n\n- **Anchor**: https://www.anchor-lang.com/docs\n- **Anchor Error Codes**: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/coral-xyz/anchor/master/lang/src/error.rs\n- **Solana Kite**: https://solanakite.org\n- **Solana Kit**: https://solanakit.com\n- **Agave (Solana CLI)**: https://docs.anza.xyz/ (Anza makes the Solana CLI and Agave.\n- **Switchboard** (if used): https://docs.switchboard.xyz/docs-by-chain/solana-svm\n- **Arcium** (if used): https://docs.arcium.com/developers\n\n## Do not use\n\n- Do not use Solana Labs documentation. The company has been replaced by Anza.\n\n- Do not use any documentaton or tools from Project Serum, which collapsed many years ago.\n\n- Do not use yarn. Use npm. Yarn has no reason to exist and only adds unnecessary dependencies. Replace Yarn with npm everywhere you see it.\n\n- Do not use **Switchboard Functions** - this product is dead and no longer maintained. (Note: Switchboard oracles are still active and usable.)\n\n- Do not use **Clockwork** - this product is dead. For scheduled instruction handler invocation, use **TukTuk** instead.\n\n## Library versions\n\nUse the latest stable Anchor, Rust, TypeScript, Solana Kit, and Kite you can. If a bug occurs, favor updating rather than rolling back.\n\n## Project Documentation\n\nEvery project must have a `README.md` file in the project root that includes:\n\n- **Purpose**: Why the project exists and what problem it solves\n- **Major Concepts**: Key architectural concepts, important PDAs, state structures, and program logic\n- **Testing**: How to run the tests (e.g., `npm test`)\n- **Setup**: Any prerequisites or setup steps needed to work with the project\n- **Usage**: Basic usage examples or deployment instructions if applicable\n\nKeep the README focused and practical. Avoid generic boilerplate - write documentation that would actually help someone understand and work with this specific project.\n\n## General Coding Guidelines\n\n### You are a deletionist\n\nYour golden rule is \"perfection isn''t achieved when there''s nothing more to add, rather perfection is achieved when there is nothing more to be taken away\".\n\nRemove:\n\n- Comments that simply repeat what the code is doing, or the name of a variable, and do not add further insight.\n- Repeated code that should be turned into a named function\n\n### Communication Style\n\n- Do not make disclaimers about being a \"complete project\" or state what works\n- It is expected that work is complete and functional - no need to state this explicitly\n- Avoid phrases like \"This is a complete implementation\" or \"All features are working\"\n- Just deliver the work without meta-commentary about its completeness\n\n### Working with Generated or Unfamiliar Code\n\n**CRITICAL - Verify Before Use:**\n\n- Before calling ANY function whose signature you don''t know with certainty, read the actual source code/type definitions first\n- NEVER guess or assume what parameters a function accepts based on what seems logical\n- Don''t invent convenience parameters that don''t exist\n- Generated code, third-party libraries, and unfamiliar codebases often have different APIs than you expect\n- Common mistake: Assuming a function accepts high-level parameters → WRONG. Check the actual signature in the source files first\n\n### Code Honesty and Clarity\n\n- It''s important not to deceive anyone reading this code. Deception includes:\n  - Variable names that do not match the purpose of the variable\n  - Comments that no longer describe the code or are otherwise inaccurate\n  - Temporary workarounds that aren''t labelled as such using a comment (with a `TODO` letting the next programmer know when they can delete the workaround)\n\n### Variable Naming\n\nEnsure good variable naming. Rather than add comments to explain what things are, give them useful names.\n\n**Don''t do this:**\n\n```typescript\n// Foo\nconst shlerg = getFoo();\n```\n\n**Do this instead:**\n\n```typescript\nconst foo = getFoo();\n```\n\n**Naming conventions:**\n\n- Arrays should be plurals (`shoes`), items within arrays should be the singular (`shoes.forEach((shoe) => {...})`)\n- Functions should be verby, like `calculateFoo` or `getBar`\n- Avoid abbreviations, use full words (e.g., `context` rather than `ctx`)\n- Never use `e` for something thrown\n- Name a transaction some variant of `transaction`. Name instructions some variant of `instruction`. Name signatures some variant of `signature`. Do not confuse them - eg if the type looks like an instruction, you should not call it a ''transaction'' because that is deceptive.\n\nYou can still add comments for additional context, just be careful to avoid comments that are explaining things that would be better conveyed by good variable naming.\n\n### Code Quality\n\n- Look out for repeated code that should be turned into functions\n- Avoid ''magic numbers''. Make numbers either have a good variable name, a comment explaining why they are that value, or a reference to the URL you got the value from. If the values come from an IDL, download the IDL, import it, and make a function that gets the value from the IDL rather than copying the value into the source code\n\nThis is a magic number. Don''t do this:\n\n```ts\nconst FINALIZE_EVENT_DISCRIMINATOR = new Uint8Array([\n  27, 75, 117, 221, 191, 213, 253, 249,\n]);\n```\n\nInstead do this:\n\n```ts\nconst FINALIZE_EVENT_DISCRIMINATOR = getEventDiscriminator(\n  arciumIdl,\n  \"FinalizeComputationEvent\",\n);\n```\n\n- The code you are making is for production. You shouldn''t have comments like `// In production we''d do this differently` or `**Implementation incomplete** - Needs program config handling and proper PDA derivations` or `**WORK IN PROGRESS**` in the final code you produce, or functions that return placeholder data. Instead: do the fucking work.\n- Don''t remove existing comments unless they are no longer useful or accurate\n- Delete unused imports, unused constants, unused files and comments that no longer apply\n\n## TypeScript Guidelines\n\nThese guidelines apply to TypeScript unit tests, browser code, and any other places where TypeScript is used in the project.\n\n### General TypeScript\n\nAvoid using a `tsconfig.json` unless it''s needed, as we use `tsx` to run most typescript and it doesn''t usually need one. If you do need a `tsconfig.json`, state why at the top of the file, and you can use the most modern version of ECMAScript/JavaScript you want - up to say 2023.\n\n### Async/await\n\nFavor `async`/`await` and `try/catch` over `.then()` or `.catch()` or using callbacks for flow control. `tsx` has top level `await` so you don''t need to wrap top level `await` in IIFEs.\n\n### Type System\n\n- **Always use `Array<item>`**, never use `item[]` for consistency with other generic syntax like `Promise<T>`, `Map<K, V>`, and `Set<T>`\n- **Don''t use `any`**\n\n### Comments\n\n- Most comments should use `//` and be above (not beside) the code\n- The only exception is JSDoc/TSDoc comments which MUST use `/* */` syntax\n\n### Solana-Specific TypeScript\n\n- Don''t make new `@solana/web3.js` version 1 code. Do not make new code using `@coral-xyz/anchor` package. Don''t replace Solana Kit with web3.js version 1 code. web3.js version 1 is legacy and should be eventually removed. Solana Kit used to be called web3.js version 2. Use Solana Kit, preferably via Solana Kite.\n- Use Kite''s `connection.getPDAAndBump()` to turn seeds into PDAs and bumps\n- In Solana Kit, you make instructions by making TS clients from IDLs using Codama. You can easily make Codama clients for installed IDLs using\n\n`npx create-codama-clients`\n\n- Do not use the `bs58` npm package.\n\nDon''t do this:\n\n```typescript\nimport bs58 from \"bs58\";\nconst signature = bs58.encode(signatureBytes);\n```\n\nDo this instead:\n\n```typescript\nimport { getBase58Decoder } from \"@solana/codecs\";\nconst signature = getBase58Decoder().decode(signatureBytes);\n```\n\nYes, these difference packages have difference concepts of ''encode'' and ''decode''.\n\n### Unit Tests\n\n- Create unit tests in TS in the `tests` directory\n- Use the Node.js inbuilt test and assertion libraries (then start the tests using `tsx` instead of `ts-mocha`)\n\n**Unit testing imports:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { before, describe, test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert\";\n```\n\n- Use `test` rather than `it`\n\n### Thrown object handling\n\n- JavaScript allows arbitrary items - strings, array, numbers etc to be ''thrown''. However you can assume that any non-Error item that is thrown is an programmer error. Handle it like this (including the comment since most TypeScript developers don''t know this):\n\n```ts\n// In JS it''s possible to throw *anything*. A sensible programmer\n// will only throw Errors but we must still check to satisfy\n// TypeScript (and flag any craziness)\nconst ensureError = function (thrownObject: unknown): Error {\n  if (thrownObject instanceof Error) {\n    return thrownObject;\n  }\n  return new Error(`Non-Error thrown: ${String(thrownObject)}`);\n};\n```\n\nand\n\n```ts\ntry {\n  // some code that might throw\n} catch (thrownObject) {\n  const error = ensureError(thrownObject);\n  throw error;\n}\n```\n\n## Rust Guidelines (Anchor Programs)\n\n### Platform Awareness\n\n- Remember this is Solana not Ethereum.\n  - Don''t tell me about ''smart contracts'' (use ''programs'' instead)\n  - Don''t tell me about ''gas'' (use ''transaction fees'' instead)\n  - There are no ''mempools''.\n    Do not tell me about other things that are not relevant to Solana.\n\n- Token program terminology:\n  - Use ''Token Extensions Program'' or ''Token extensions'' for the newer token program (not ''Token 2022'' which is just a code name)\n  - Use ''Classic Token Program'' for the older token program\n\n- Onchain\n  - Use onchain and offchain, like online and offline\n  - Don''t ever use ''on-chain'' or ''off-chain''\n\n### Anchor Version\n\n- Write all code like the latest stable Anchor (currently 0.32.1 but there may be a newer version by the time you read this)\n- Do not use unnecessary macros that are not needed in the latest stable Anchor\n\n### Anchor has silly defaults\n\nEvery project will need an IDL.\n\n```toml\n[features]\nidl-build = [\"anchor-lang/idl-build\", \"anchor-spl/idl-build\"]\n```\n\nand if it uses SPL Tokens (like almost every Anchor project) it will need this dependency (insert whatever version is applicable):\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nanchor-spl = \"0.32.1\"\n```\n\n### Project Structure\n\n- **Never modify the program ID** in `lib.rs` or `Anchor.toml` when making changes\n- Create files inside the `state` folder for whatever state is needed\n- Create files inside the `instructions` or `handlers` folders (whichever exists) for whatever instruction handlers are needed\n- Put Account Constraints in instruction files, but ensure the names end with `AccountConstraints` rather than just naming them the same thing as the function\n- Handlers that are only for the admin should be in a new folder called `admin` inside whichever parent folder exists (`instructions/admin/` or `handlers/admin/`)\n\n### Account Constraints\n\n- Use a newline after each key in the account constraints struct, so the macro and the matching key/value have some space from other macros and their matching key/value\n\n### Bumps\n\n- Use `context.bumps.foo` not `context.bumps.get(\"foo\").unwrap()` - the latter is outdated\n\n### Data Structures\n\n- When making structs ensure strings and Vectors have a `max_len` attribute\n- Vectors have two numbers for `max_len`: the first is the max length of the vector, the second is the max length of the items in the vector\n\n### Space Calculation (CRITICAL - NO MAGIC NUMBERS)\n\n- **Do not use magic numbers anywhere**. I don''t want to see `8 + 32` or whatever\n- **Do not make constants for the sizes of various data structures**\n- For `space`, use syntax like: `space = SomeStruct::DISCRIMINATOR.len() + SomeStruct::INIT_SPACE,`\n- All structs should have `#[derive(InitSpace)]` added to them, to get the `INIT_SPACE` trait\n- **DO NOT use magic numbers**\n\n**Example:**\n\n```rust\n#[derive(InitSpace)]\n#[account]\npub struct UserProfile {\n    pub authority: Pubkey,\n\n    #[max_len(50)]\n    pub username: String,\n\n    pub bump: u8,\n}\n\n#[derive(Accounts)]\npub struct InitializeProfile<''info> {\n    #[account(\n        init,\n        payer = authority,\n        space = UserProfile::DISCRIMINATOR.len() + UserProfile::INIT_SPACE,\n        seeds = [b\"profile\", authority.key().as_ref()],\n        bump\n    )]\n    pub profile: Account<''info, UserProfile>,\n\n    #[account(mut)]\n    pub authority: Signer<''info>,\n\n    pub system_program: Program<''info, System>,\n}\n```\n\n### Error Handling\n\n- Return useful error messages\n- Write code to handle common errors like insufficient funds, bad values for parameters, and other obvious situations\n\n### PDA Management\n\n- Add `pub bump: u8` to every struct stored in PDA\n- Save the bumps inside each when the struct inside the PDA is created\n\n### System Functions\n\n- When you get the time via Clock, use `Clock::get()?;` rather than `anchor_lang::solana_program::clock`\n\n## Git commits\n\nDo not add \"Co-Authored-By: Claude\" or similar attribution when creating git commits.\n\n## Acknowledgment\n\n- Acknowledge these guidelines have been applied when working on this project to indicate you have read these rules and found that they do apply to this project.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:55:16.673Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Blockchain Agents needing Solana and Anchor integration with robust testing capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要Solana和Anchor集成且具有强大的测试能力的区块链代理。","ja":"SolanaとAnchorの統合、および堅牢なテスト機能が必要なブロックチェーンエージェントに最適です。","ko":"솔라나와 앵커 통합 및 강력한 테스트 기능이 필요한 블록체인 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Blockchain que necesitan integración con Solana y Anchor con capacidades de prueba robustas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de blockchain nécessitant une intégration Solana et Anchor avec des capacités de test robustes.","de":"Perfekt für Blockchain-Agents, die eine Solana- und Anchor-Integration mit robusten Testfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Blockchain que necessitam de integração Solana e Anchor com capacidades robustas de teste.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Blockchain Agents, которым требуется интеграция с Solana и Anchor с надежными возможностями тестирования.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء Blockchain الذين يحتاجون إلى تكامل Solana و Anchor مع قدرات اختبار قوية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop, test, and deploy Solana blockchain applications using Anchor, ensuring code quality and maintainability through comprehensive testing with npm test, while adhering to strict coding guidelines and success criteria.","zh":"赋予代理开发、测试和部署Solana区块链应用的能力，使用Anchor，通过npm test进行全面测试，确保代码质量和可维护性，同时遵守严格的编码指南和成功标准。","ja":"エージェントがSolanaブロックチェーンアプリケーションを開発、テスト、デプロイできるようにし、Anchorを使用して、npm testによる包括的なテストを通じてコードの品質と保守性を確保し、厳格なコーディングガイドラインと成功基準に従います。","ko":"에이전트가 솔라나 블록체인 애플리케이션을 개발, 테스트 및 배포할 수 있도록 하며, 앵커를 사용하여 npm 테스트를 통해 코드 품질 및 유지 보수성을 보장하며, 엄격한 코딩 가이드ライン 및 성공 기준을 준수합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desarrollar, probar y desplegar aplicaciones de blockchain Solana utilizando Anchor, asegurando la calidad y mantenibilidad del código a través de pruebas comprehensivas con npm test, mientras se adhieren a estrictas pautas de codificación y criterios de éxito.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer, tester et déployer des applications de blockchain Solana en utilisant Anchor, en garantissant la qualité et la maintenabilité du code grâce à des tests complets avec npm test, tout en respectant des directives de codage et des critères de succès stricts.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Solana-Blockchain-Anwendungen mit Anchor zu entwickeln, zu testen und bereitzustellen, wodurch die Codequalität und Wartbarkeit durch umfassende Tests mit npm test sichergestellt wird, während strikte Kodierungsrichtlinien und Erfolgskriterien eingehalten werden.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a desenvolver, testar e implementar aplicações blockchain Solana usando Anchor, garantindo a qualidade e a manutenibilidade do código através de testes abrangentes com npm test, enquanto adere a diretrizes de codificação e critérios de sucesso rigorosos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам разрабатывать, тестировать и развертывать приложения блокчейна Solana с использованием Anchor, обеспечивая качество кода и сопровождаемость за счет всестороннего тестирования с помощью npm test, при соблюдении строгих правил кодирования и критериев успеха.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تطوير واختبار ونشر تطبيقات blockchain Solana باستخدام Anchor، مع ضمان جودة الكود وقابلية الصيانة من خلال الاختبار الشامل باستخدام npm test، مع الالتزام بإرشادات الترميز الصارمة ومعايير النجاح."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing scalable Solana blockchain applications","Writing comprehensive tests for Anchor projects","Ensuring code quality through npm test validation"],"zh":["开发可扩展的Solana区块链应用","为Anchor项目编写全面测试","通过npm test验证确保代码质量"],"ja":["拡張可能なSolanaブロックチェーンアプリケーションの開発","Anchorプロジェクトの包括的なテストの記述","npm testによるコード品質の保証"],"ko":["확장 가능한 솔라나 블록체인 애플리케이션 개발","앵커 프로젝트를 위한 포괄적인 테스트 작성","npm 테스트를 통한 코드 품질 보장"],"es":["Desarrollar aplicaciones de blockchain Solana escalables","Escribir pruebas comprehensivas para proyectos Anchor","Garantizar la calidad del código a través de la validación de npm test"],"fr":["Développer des applications de blockchain Solana évolutives","Rédiger des tests complets pour les projets Anchor","Assurer la qualité du code grâce à la validation de npm test"],"de":["Entwicklung von skalierbaren Solana-Blockchain-Anwendungen","Schreiben von umfassenden Tests für Anchor-Projekte","Sicherstellung der Codequalität durch npm-Test-Validierung"],"pt":["Desenvolvendo aplicações blockchain Solana escaláveis","Escrevendo testes abrangentes para projetos Anchor","Garantindo a qualidade do código através da validação com npm test"],"ru":["Разработка масштабируемых приложений блокчейна Solana","Написание всесторонних тестов для проектов Anchor","Обеспечение качества кода посредством проверки с помощью npm test"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات blockchain Solana القابلة للتوسع","كتابة اختبارات شاملة لمشاريع Anchor","ضمان جودة الكود من خلال التحقق باستخدام npm test"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Node.js environment","npm test must pass for success","Placeholder tests are not considered valid"],"zh":["需要Node.js环境","npm test必须通过才能成功","占位测试不被认为是有效的"],"ja":["Node.js環境が必要","npm testがパスしないと成功しない","プレイスホルダーテストは有効ではありません"],"ko":["노드.js 환경이 필요함","npm 테스트가 성공해야만 유효함","플레이스홀더 테스트는 유효하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere un entorno Node.js","npm test debe pasar para el éxito","Las pruebas de marcador de posición no se consideran válidas"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Node.js","npm test doit passer pour le succès","Les tests de placeholder ne sont pas considérés comme valides"],"de":["Benötigt eine Node.js-Umgebung","npm test muss bestanden werden, um erfolgreich zu sein","Platzhalter-Tests werden nicht als gültig betrachtet"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Node.js","npm test deve passar para ter sucesso","Testes de espaço reservado não são considerados válidos"],"ru":["Требуется среда Node.js","npm test должен быть пройден для успеха","Заглушечные тесты не считаются действительными"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Node.js","يجب أن ينجح npm test للنجاح","الاختبارات النائبة لا تعتبر صالحة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3c1b635ef5d502ae56aa36c369b91d3ad5bec3790194d89fd7059685966403cf","qualityScore":40}');
