ienz bei der Code-Ausführung","Lösung für Anwendungs-Entwickler","Unterstützung für die Erstellung von skalierbaren Anwendungen"],"pt":["Runtime TypeScript nativo para Zig","Melhoria da eficiência do desenvolvimento","Porta do mquickjs","Cresceu para algo maior","Suporte a desenvolvimento de aplicações"],"ru":["Родной TypeScript Runtime для Zig","Улучшение эффективности разработки","Порт mquickjs","Вырос в что-то большее","Поддержка разработки приложений"],"ar":["وقت تشغيل TypeScript الأصلي لمحرك Zig","تحسين كفاءة التطوير","بورت مفتوح لمحرك mquickjs","أصبح أكبر","دعم تطوير التطبيقات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Zig Expert","原生 TypeScript 运行时","高性能计算","开发者工具","TypeScript 教程","Zig vs Rust","如何使用 Zig","Zig 安装指南"],"ja":["Zig エキスパート","ネイティブ TypeScript ランタイム","高速計算","開発者ツール","TypeScript ガイド","Zig vs Rust","Zig の使い方","Zig インストールガイド"],"ko":["Zig 전문가","네이티브 TypeScript 런타임","고성능 계산","개발자 도구","TypeScript 튜토리얼","Zig vs Rust","Zig 사용법","Zig 설치 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar Zig","qué es TypeScript","alternativas a mquickjs","Zig vs mquickjs","instalación de Zig","guía de configuración de Zig","desarrollo de aplicaciones con Zig","mejores prácticas para Zig"],"fr":["comment utiliser Zig","quoi est TypeScript","alternatives à mquickjs","Zig vs mquickjs","installation de Zig","guide de configuration de Zig","développement d''applications avec Zig","meilleures pratiques pour Zig"],"de":["wie man Zig verwendet","was ist TypeScript","Alternativen zu mquickjs","Zig vs mquickjs","Installation von Zig","Konfigurationsanleitung für Zig","Anwendungsentwicklung mit Zig","Best Practices für Zig"],"pt":["como usar zig-expert","o que é zig-expert","alternativa ao mquickjs","zig-expert vs mquickjs","instalar zig-expert","guia de configuração do zig-expert","desenvolvimento de aplicações com zig-expert"],"ru":["как использовать zig-expert","что такое zig-expert","альтернатива mquickjs","zig-expert vs mquickjs","установить zig-expert","руководство по настройке zig-expert","разработка приложений с помощью zig-expert"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة zig-expert","ما هي أداة zig-expert","بديل لمحرك mquickjs","أداة zig-expert مقابل محرك mquickjs","تثبيت أداة zig-expert","دليل إعداد أداة zig-expert","تطوير التطبيقات باستخدام أداة zig-expert"]}},"owner":"srdjan","repo":"zigttp","repoPath":"srdjan/zigttp","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.990Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"zig-expert","description":"Write idiomatic Zig code following the Zen of Zig philosophy. Use for systems programming with Zig (.zig files), covering manual memory management with allocators, error unions and explicit error handling, compile-time programming (comptime), data-oriented design, and the new async/Io model. Applies functional programming parallels (Result types, ADTs, explicit effects) for C-free systems development.","bodyPreview":"# Idiomatic Zig Programming\n\nExpert guidance for writing idiomatic Zig code that embodies the Zen of Zig: explicit intent, no hidden control flow, and compile-time over runtime.\n\n## Zen of Zig (Core Philosophy)\n\nThese principles govern all idiomatic Zig code:\n\n| Principle | Implication |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Communicate intent precisely | Explicit code; APIs make requirements obvious |\n| Edge cases matter | No undefined behaviors glossed over |\n| Favor reading over writing | Optimize fo","body":"# Idiomatic Zig Programming\n\nExpert guidance for writing idiomatic Zig code that embodies the Zen of Zig: explicit intent, no hidden control flow, and compile-time over runtime.\n\n## Zen of Zig (Core Philosophy)\n\nThese principles govern all idiomatic Zig code:\n\n| Principle | Implication |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Communicate intent precisely | Explicit code; APIs make requirements obvious |\n| Edge cases matter | No undefined behaviors glossed over |\n| Favor reading over writing | Optimize for clarity and maintainability |\n| One obvious way | Avoid multiple complex features for same task |\n| Runtime crashes > bugs | Fail fast and loudly, never corrupt state silently |\n| Compile errors > runtime crashes | Catch issues at compile-time when possible |\n| Resource deallocation must succeed | Design APIs with allocation failure in mind |\n| Memory is a resource | Manage memory as consciously as any other resource |\n| No hidden control flow | No exceptions, no GC, no implicit allocations |\n\n## FP Conceptual Parallels\n\nZig shares key concepts with functional programming:\n\n| FP Concept | Zig Equivalent |\n|------------|----------------|\n| Result/Either type | Error union `!T` (either error or value) |\n| Option/Maybe | Optional `?T` (nullable type) |\n| ADTs / Sum types | Tagged unions with `union(enum)` |\n| Pattern matching | `switch` with exhaustive handling |\n| Explicit effects | Allocator/Io parameters (dependency injection) |\n| Immutability preference | `const` by default, `var` only when needed |\n| Pure functions | Functions without hidden state or allocations |\n\n## Workflow Decision Tree\n\n1. **Declaring a binding?** → Use `const` unless mutation required\n2. **Function needs memory?** → Accept `Allocator` parameter, never global alloc\n3. **Function can fail?** → Return error union `!T`, use `try` to propagate\n4. **Handling an error?** → Use `catch` with explicit handler or `try` to propagate\n5. **Need cleanup on exit?** → Use `defer` immediately after acquisition\n6. **Cleanup only on error?** → Use `errdefer` for conditional cleanup\n7. **Need generic code?** → Use `comptime` type parameters\n8. **Compile-time known value?** → Use `comptime` to evaluate at build time\n9. **Calling C code?** → Use `@cImport` for seamless FFI\n10. **Need async I/O?** → Pass `Io` interface, use `io.async()` and `future.await()`\n11. **Optimizing hot path?** → Consider data-oriented design (SoA vs AoS)\n\n## Essential Patterns\n\n### Error Unions (Result Type Equivalent)\n\n```zig\nconst FileError = error{ NotFound, PermissionDenied, InvalidPath };\n\nfn readConfig(path: []const u8) FileError!Config {\n    const file = std.fs.cwd().openFile(path, .{}) catch |err| {\n        return switch (err) {\n            error.FileNotFound => error.NotFound,\n            error.AccessDenied => error.PermissionDenied,\n            else => error.InvalidPath,\n        };\n    };\n    defer file.close();\n    // ... parse config\n    return config;\n}\n\n// Propagate with try (like Rust''s ?)\npub fn main() !void {\n    const config = try readConfig(\"app.conf\");\n    // ...\n}\n\n// Handle explicitly with catch\npub fn mainSafe() void {\n    const config = readConfig(\"app.conf\") catch |err| {\n        std.debug.print(\"Failed: {}\\n\", .{err});\n        return;\n    };\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Allocator Pattern (Explicit Effects)\n\n```zig\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\n\n// Function signature communicates: \"I need to allocate\"\nfn processData(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, input: []const u8) ![]u8 {\n    var result = try allocator.alloc(u8, input.len * 2);\n    errdefer allocator.free(result); // cleanup only on error path\n    \n    // ... process into result\n    \n    return result; // caller owns this memory\n}\n\npub fn main() !void {\n    var gpa = std.heap.GeneralPurposeAllocator(.{}){};\n    defer _ = gpa.deinit();\n    const allocator = gpa.allocator();\n    \n    const data = try processData(allocator, \"input\");\n    defer allocator.free(data); // caller responsible for cleanup\n}\n```\n\n### Tagged Unions (ADTs / Sum Types)\n\n```zig\nconst PaymentState = union(enum) {\n    pending: void,\n    processing: struct { transaction_id: []const u8 },\n    completed: Receipt,\n    failed: PaymentError,\n    \n    // Methods on the union\n    pub fn describe(self: PaymentState) []const u8 {\n        return switch (self) {\n            .pending => \"Waiting for payment\",\n            .processing => |p| p.transaction_id,\n            .completed => |r| r.summary,\n            .failed => |e| e.message,\n        };\n    }\n};\n\n// Exhaustive switch (compiler enforces all cases)\nfn handlePayment(state: PaymentState) void {\n    switch (state) {\n        .pending => startProcessing(),\n        .processing => |p| pollStatus(p.transaction_id),\n        .completed => |receipt| sendConfirmation(receipt),\n        .failed => |err| notifyFailure(err),\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Compile-Time Programming\n\n```zig\n// comptime function for generics\nfn max(comptime T: type, a: T, b: T) T {\n    return if (a > b) a else b;\n}\n\n// Compile-time computed constants\nconst LOOKUP_TABLE = blk: {\n    var table: [256]u8 = undefined;\n    for (&table, 0..) |*entry, i| {\n        entry.* = @intCast((i * 7) % 256);\n    }\n    break :blk table;\n};\n\n// Generic container (like TypeScript generics)\nfn ArrayList(comptime T: type) type {\n    return struct {\n        items: []T,\n        allocator: std.mem.Allocator,\n        \n        const Self = @This();\n        \n        pub fn init(allocator: std.mem.Allocator) Self {\n            return .{ .items = &[_]T{}, .allocator = allocator };\n        }\n        \n        pub fn append(self: *Self, item: T) !void {\n            // ...\n        }\n    };\n}\n```\n\n### Resource Management with defer\n\n```zig\nfn processFile(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, path: []const u8) !void {\n    // Open file\n    const file = try std.fs.cwd().openFile(path, .{});\n    defer file.close(); // ALWAYS runs on scope exit\n    \n    // Allocate buffer\n    const buffer = try allocator.alloc(u8, 4096);\n    defer allocator.free(buffer); // cleanup guaranteed\n    \n    // errdefer for conditional cleanup\n    var result = try allocator.alloc(u8, 1024);\n    errdefer allocator.free(result); // only on error\n    \n    // If we reach here successfully, caller owns result\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```zig\n// Imports\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\n\n// Variables\nconst immutable: u32 = 42;        // prefer const\nvar mutable: u32 = 0;             // only when needed\n\n// Optionals (?T) - like Option/Maybe\nvar maybe_value: ?u32 = null;\nconst unwrapped = maybe_value orelse 0;        // default value\nconst ptr = maybe_value orelse return error.Missing;  // early return\n\n// Error unions (!T) - like Result/Either\nfn canFail() !u32 { return error.SomeError; }\nconst value = try canFail();                   // propagate error\nconst safe = canFail() catch |err| handleError(err);  // catch error\n\n// Slices (pointer + length, not null-terminated)\nconst slice: []const u8 = \"hello\";             // string literal is []const u8\nconst arr: [5]u8 = .{ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };\nconst sub = arr[1..3];                         // slice of array\n\n// Iteration\nfor (slice, 0..) |byte, index| { }             // value and index\nfor (slice) |byte| { }                         // value only\n\n// Switch (exhaustive, can capture)\nswitch (tagged_union) {\n    .variant => |captured| doSomething(captured),\n    else => {},  // or handle all cases\n}\n\n// Comptime\nconst SIZE = comptime blk: { break :blk 64; };\nfn generic(comptime T: type, val: T) T { return val; }\n```\n\n## Detailed References\n\n- **[references/idioms.md](references/idioms.md)** - Data-oriented design, memory patterns, testing\n- **[references/async-io.md](references/async-io.md)** - New async/Io model, futures, cancellation\n- **[references/c-interop.md](references/c-interop.md)** - C FFI, @cImport, ABI compatibility\n\n## Forbidden Patterns\n\n| ❌ Never | ✅ Instead |\n|----------|-----------|\n| Global allocator / hidden malloc | Pass `Allocator` explicitly |\n| Exceptions / panic for errors | Return error union `!T` |\n| Null pointers without type | Use optional `?*T` |\n| Preprocessor macros | Use `comptime` and inline functions |\n| C-style strings in Zig code | Use slices `[]const u8` |\n| Ignoring errors silently | Handle with `catch` or propagate with `try` |\n| `var` when `const` works | Default to `const`, mutate only when necessary |\n| Hidden control flow | Make all branches explicit |\n| OOP inheritance hierarchies | Use composition and tagged unions |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:02:30.726Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents requiring native Zig runtime execution and compile-time code analysis capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要原生Zig运行时执行和编译时代码分析能力的AI代理。","ja":"ネイティブのZigランタイム実行とコンパイル時コード分析機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"원生的 Zig 런타임 실행 및 컴파일 시간 코드 분석 기능을 필요로 하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que requieren ejecución de tiempo de ejecución de Zig nativa y capacidades de análisis de código de tiempo de compilación.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant une exécution native de runtime Zig et des capacités d''analyse de code à temps de compilation.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die eine native Zig-Laufzeit-Ausführung und Compile-Time-Code-Analysefunktionen erfordern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que requerem execução nativa do runtime Zig e capacidades de análise de código em tempo de compilação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-агентов, требующих нативного выполнения среды выполнения Zig и возможностей анализа кода во время компиляции.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يتطلبون تنفيذ وقت تشغيل Zig الأصلي وقدرات تحليل الكود في وقت الترجمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to execute Zig code natively through TypeScript runtime integration, providing expert guidance on idiomatic Zig programming principles including explicit intent communication and compile-time optimization over runtime. The skill specifically handles edge cases and undefined behaviors while maintaining the Zen of Zig philosophy.","zh":"通过TypeScript运行时集成，使代理能够本地执行Zig代码，提供关于习惯用Zig编程原则（包括显式意图通信和编译时优化优于运行时）的专家指导。该技能特别处理边缘情况和未定义行为，同时保持Zig的禅宗哲学。","ja":"TypeScriptランタイム統合を通じて、エージェントがZigコードをネイティブに実行できるようにし、明示的な意図の伝達やコンパイル時最適化などZigプログラミングの原則に関する専門家のガイダンスを提供します。このスキルは、Zigの禅の哲学を維持しながら、エッジケースや未定義の動作を特に処理します。","ko":"TypeScript 런타임 통합을 통해 에이전트가 Zig 코드를 네이티브로 실행할 수 있도록 하며, 명시적인 의도 전달 및 컴파일 시간 최적화와 같은 Zig 프로그래밍 원칙에 대한 전문가의 가이드를 제공합니다. 이 스킬은 Zig의 禅의 철학을 유지하면서 에지 케이스 및 정의되지 않은 동작을 특히 처리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar código Zig de forma nativa a través de la integración de tiempo de ejecución de TypeScript, proporcionando orientación experta sobre principios de programación Zig idiomáticos, incluida la comunicación de intención explícita y la optimización de tiempo de compilación sobre tiempo de ejecución. La habilidad maneja específicamente casos de borde y comportamientos no definidos mientras mantiene la filosofía Zen de Zig.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter du code Zig de manière native via l''intégration de runtime TypeScript, fournissant une orientation experte sur les principes de programmation Zig idiomatiques, y compris la communication d''intention explicite et l''optimisation à temps de compilation sur le runtime. La compétence gère spécifiquement les cas limites et les comportements non définis tout en maintenant la philosophie Zen de Zig.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Zig-Code nativ über die TypeScript-Laufzeit-Integration auszuführen und bietet Expertenrat zu idiomatischen Zig-Programmierprinzipien, einschließlich expliziter Intent-Kommunikation und Compile-Time-Optimierung über Laufzeit. Die Fähigkeit behandelt speziell Randfälle und undefiniertes Verhalten, während sie die Zen-Philosophie von Zig beibehält.","pt":"Permite que os agentes executem código Zig nativamente através da integração com o runtime TypeScript, fornecendo orientação especializada sobre os princípios idiomáticos de programação Zig, incluindo comunicação explícita de intenção e otimização em tempo de compilação em vez de runtime. A skill lida especificamente com casos extremos e comportamentos indefinidos, mantendo a filosofia Zen do Zig.","ru":"Позволяет агентам нативно выполнять код Zig через интеграцию со средой выполнения TypeScript, предоставляя экспертное руководство по идиоматическим принципам программирования Zig, включая явную коммуникацию намерений и оптимизацию во время компиляции вместо выполнения. Навык специально обрабатывает крайние случаи и неопределенное поведение, сохраняя философию Zen of Zig.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تنفيذ كود Zig أصليًا من خلال تكامل وقت تشغيل TypeScript، ويوفر توجيهًا خبيرًا حول مبادئ البرمجة الاصطلاحية في Zig بما في ذلك التواصل الصريح للنية والتحسين في وقت الترجمة بدلاً وقت التشغيل. تتناول المهارة على وجه التحديد الحالات المتطرفة والسلوكيات غير المعرفة مع الحفاظ على فلسفة Zen of Zig."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing Zig code for idiomatic patterns","Validating compile-time optimization opportunities","Detecting hidden control flow in Zig implementations","Generating edge case test scenarios for Zig modules"],"zh":["分析Zig代码中的习惯用模式","验证编译时优化机会","检测Zig实现中的隐式控制流","为Zig模块生成边缘情况测试场景"],"ja":["Zigコードの慣用パターンを分析する","コンパイル時最適化の機会を検証する","Zig実装における隠れた制御フローを検出する","Zigモジュールのエッジケーステストシナリオを生成する"],"ko":["Zig 코드의 관용적인 패턴을 분석하는 것","컴파일 시간 최적화 기회를 검증하는 것","Zig 구현의 숨겨진 제어 흐름을 감지하는 것","Zig 모듈의 에지 케이스 테스트 시나리오를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Analizar código Zig para patrones idiomáticos","Validar oportunidades de optimización de tiempo de compilación","Detectar flujo de control oculto en implementaciones de Zig","Generar escenarios de prueba de casos de borde para módulos de Zig"],"fr":["Analyser le code Zig pour les modèles idiomatiques","Valider les opportunités d''optimisation à temps de compilation","Détecter le flux de contrôle caché dans les implementations Zig","Générer des scénarios de test de cas de limite pour les modules Zig"],"de":["Zig-Code für idiomatische Muster analysieren","Optimierungsmöglichkeiten zur Compile-Time überprüfen","Versteckten Kontrollfluss in Zig-Implementierungen erkennen","Testfall-Szenarien für Zig-Module generieren"],"pt":["Analisar código Zig em busca de padrões idiomáticos","Validar oportunidades de otimização em tempo de compilação","Detectar fluxo de controle oculto em implementações Zig","Gerar cenários de teste para casos extremos em módulos Zig"],"ru":["Анализ кода Zig на предмет идиоматических шаблонов","Проверка возможностей оптимизации во время компиляции","Обнаружение скрытого потока управления в реализациях Zig","Генерация сценариев тестирования для крайних случаев в модулях Zig"],"ar":["تحليل كود Zig للأنماط الاصطلاحية","التحقق من فرص التحسين في وقت الترجمة","الكشف عن تدفق التحكم المخفي في تطبيقات Zig","إنشاء سيناريوهات اختبار للحالات المتطرفة لوحدات Zig"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Zig runtime environment","Limited to Zig-specific code analysis","Depends on native TypeScript runtime integration"],"zh":["需要Zig运行时环境","仅限于Zig特定的代码分析","依赖于原生的TypeScript运行时集成"],"ja":["Zigランタイム環境が必要","Zig特有のコード分析に限定される","ネイティブのTypeScriptランタイム統合に依存する"],"ko":["Zig 런타임 환경이 필요","Zig 특정 코드 분석으로 제한","원生的 TypeScript 런타임 통합에 의존"],"es":["Requiere entorno de tiempo de ejecución de Zig","Limitado al análisis de código específico de Zig","Depende de la integración de tiempo de ejecución de TypeScript nativa"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement de runtime Zig","Limité à l''analyse de code spécifique à Zig","Dépend de l''intégration de runtime TypeScript native"],"de":["Benötigt Zig-Laufzeitumgebung","Begrenzt auf Zig-spezifische Code-Analyse","Hängt von der nativen TypeScript-Laufzeit-Integration ab"],"pt":["Requer ambiente de runtime Zig","Limitado à análise de código específica do Zig","Depende da integração nativa com o runtime TypeScript"],"ru":["Требует среду выполнения Zig","Ограничен анализом кода, специфичного для Zig","Зависит от нативной интеграции со средой выполнения TypeScript"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة وقت تشغيل Zig","مقصور على تحليل الكود المخصص لـ Zig","يعتمد على التكامل الأصلي مع وقت تشغيل TypeScript"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"4e95bdb4fad789a04c1ea79dcb63ba5dcc0a679fcaff867d959346a2b89f1d44","qualityScore":39}');
