 with Codex CLI and Agent Skills"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"threejs-builder AI工具 - 3D游戏开发","ja":"threejs-builder AIエージェント - マリオパーティー ミニゲーム風","ko":"threejs-builder AI 에이전트 - 3D 게임 개발","es":"Herramientas de AI: threejs-builder para juegos 3D","fr":"Outils d''IA: threejs-builder pour jeux 3D","de":"KI-Tools: threejs-builder für 3D-Spiele","pt":"Ferramenta threejs-builder: Crie Jogos 3D com AI","ru":"ИИ Агенты: threejs-builder для создания 3D игр","ar":"اداة threejs-builder: بناء ألعاب 3D بالذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"threejs-builder"},"description":{"zh":"threejs-builder是一个使用Codex CLI和Agent Skills构建的3D游戏，灵感来自Mario Party的迷你游戏","ja":"threejs-builderは、Codex CLIとAgent Skillsを使用して構築された3Dゲームで、マリオパーティーのミニゲームにインスパイアされたものです","ko":"threejs-builder는 Codex CLI와 Agent Skills를 사용하여 구축된 3D 게임으로, Mario Party의 미니 게임에서 영감을 얻었습니다","es":"Threejs-builder es una herramienta de AI que permite crear juegos 3D inspirados en Mario Party con Codex CLI y habilidades de agente. Ideal para desarrollado...","fr":"Threejs-builder est un outil d''IA qui permet de créer des jeux 3D inspirés de Mario Party avec Codex CLI et compétences d''agent. Idéal pour les développeurs ...","de":"Threejs-builder ist ein KI-Tool, das das Erstellen von 3D-Spielen im Stil von Mario Party mit Codex CLI und Agent-Fähigkeiten ermöglicht. Ideal für Spieleent...","pt":"A ferramenta threejs-builder é uma solução para criar jogos 3D inspirados em Mario Party, feita com Codex CLI e habilidades de agente. Ela permite aos desenv...","ru":"ИИ Агент threejs-builder - это решение для создания 3D игр в стиле Mario Party, сделанное с помощью Codex CLI и навыков агента. Он позволяет разработчикам со...","ar":"أداة threejs-builder هي حل لإنشاء ألعاب 3D مستوحاة من ماريو بارتي، مصنوعة مع Codex CLI ومهارات الوكيل. وهي تسمح للمطورين بإنشاء تجارب ألعاب 3D مخصصة","en":"A vibe coded 3D game inspired by the Mario Party mini game. Made with Codex CLI and Agent Skills"},"definition":{"en":"A vibe coded 3D game inspired by the Mario Party mini game. Made with Codex CLI and Agent Skills"},"features":{"zh":["使用Codex CLI构建","Agent Skills集成","3D游戏开发","Mario Party风格","互动体验"],"ja":["Codex CLIを使用した構築","Agent Skillsの統合","3Dゲーム開発","マリオパーティー ミニゲーム風","インタラクティブ体験"],"ko":["Codex CLI를 사용한 구축","Agent Skills 통합","3D 게임 개발","Mario Party风格","상호작용 경험"],"es":["Creación de juegos 3D con Codex CLI","Inspirado en Mario Party","Utiliza habilidades de agente","Ideal para desarrolladores de juegos","Permite la creación de juegos personalizados","Fácil de usar y configurar"],"fr":["Création de jeux 3D avec Codex CLI","Inspiré de Mario Party","Utilise des compétences d''agent","Idéal pour les développeurs de jeux","Permet la création de jeux personnalisés","Facile à utiliser et à configurer"],"de":["Erstellung von 3D-Spielen mit Codex CLI","Im Stil von Mario Party","Verwendet Agent-Fähigkeiten","Ideal für Spieleentwickler","Ermöglicht die Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Spielen","Einfach zu bedienen und zu konfigurieren"],"pt":["Criação de jogos 3D personalizados","Integração com Codex CLI","Habilidades de agente para jogos 3D","Inspiração em Mario Party","Desenvolvimento rápido e fácil"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных 3D игр","Интеграция с Codex CLI","Навыки агента для 3D игр","Вдохновение от Mario Party","Быстрое и легкое развитие"],"ar":["إنشاء ألعاب 3D مخصصة","التكامل مع Codex CLI","مهارات الوكيل لألعاب 3D","الاستلهام من ماريو بارتي","التطوير السريع والسهل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["threejs-builder","AI工具","3D游戏开发","Codex CLI","Agent Skills","如何使用threejs-builder","threejs-builder教程","threejs-builder替代品"],"ja":["threejs-builder","AIエージェント","3Dゲーム開発","Codex CLI","Agent Skills","threejs-builderの使い方","threejs-builderチュートリアル","threejs-builderの代替"],"ko":["threejs-builder","AI 에이전트","3D 게임 개발","Codex CLI","Agent Skills","threejs-builder 사용법","threejs-builder 튜토리얼","threejs-builder 대안"],"es":["cómo usar threejs-builder","qué es threejs-builder","alternativas a threejs-builder","threejs-builder vs otros herramientas de AI","instalación de threejs-builder","guía de configuración de threejs-builder","desarrollo de juegos 3D con threejs-builder","herramientas de AI para juegos","threejs-builder para desarrolladores"],"fr":["comment utiliser threejs-builder","qu''est-ce que threejs-builder","alternatives à threejs-builder","threejs-builder vs autres outils d''IA","installation de threejs-builder","guide de configuration de threejs-builder","développement de jeux 3D avec threejs-builder","outils d''IA pour jeux","threejs-builder pour développeurs"],"de":["wie man threejs-builder verwendet","was ist threejs-builder","alternativen zu threejs-builder","threejs-builder vs andere KI-Tools","installation von threejs-builder","konfigurationsanleitung für threejs-builder","entwicklung von 3D-Spielen mit threejs-builder","KI-Tools für Spiele","threejs-builder für Entwickler"],"pt":["como usar threejs-builder","o que é threejs-builder","alternativa para threejs-builder","threejs-builder vs outros","instalar threejs-builder","guia de configuração threejs-builder"],"ru":["как использовать threejs-builder","что такое threejs-builder","альтернатива для threejs-builder","threejs-builder vs другие","установить threejs-builder","руководство по настройке threejs-builder"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام threejs-builder","ما هي أداة threejs-builder","بديل لأداة threejs-builder","threejs-builder مقابل الأخرى","تثبيت threejs-builder","دليل إعداد threejs-builder"]}},"owner":"chongdashu","repo":"threejs-forest-census","repoPath":"chongdashu/threejs-forest-census","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.993Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"threejs-builder","description":"Design and implement lightweight Three.js (r150+) ES-module scenes—hero sections, interactive product viewers, particle backdrops, GLTF showcases, or quick prototypes—whenever prompts mention three.js/threejs scene, 3D web background, orbit controls, or WebGL demo.","bodyPreview":"# Three.js Builder\n\nA Codex-ready framework for shipping elegant, performant Three.js web experiences with modern ES modules.\n\n## Reference Files\n\n> **Read the appropriate reference when working on specific topics:**\n\n| Topic | File | Use When |\n|-------|------|----------|\n| **GLTF Models** | `references/gltf-loading-guide.md` | Loading, caching, cloning 3D models, SkeletonUtils |\n| **Reference Frames** | `references/reference-frame-contract.md` | Calibration, anchoring, axis correctness, debugg","body":"# Three.js Builder\n\nA Codex-ready framework for shipping elegant, performant Three.js web experiences with modern ES modules.\n\n## Reference Files\n\n> **Read the appropriate reference when working on specific topics:**\n\n| Topic | File | Use When |\n|-------|------|----------|\n| **GLTF Models** | `references/gltf-loading-guide.md` | Loading, caching, cloning 3D models, SkeletonUtils |\n| **Reference Frames** | `references/reference-frame-contract.md` | Calibration, anchoring, axis correctness, debugging |\n| **Game Development** | `references/game-patterns.md` | State machines, animation switching, parallax, pooling |\n| **Advanced Topics** | `references/advanced-topics.md` | Post-processing, shaders, physics, instancing |\n| **Calibration Helpers** | `scripts/README.md` | GLTF calibration helper installation and usage |\n\n---\n\n## Philosophy: Start from Scene Intent\n\nThree.js work lives inside a scene graph: parents transform children, and everything in `scene` is rendered.\n\n**Before writing code, ask**:\n- What is the core visual element or metaphor (hero object, particle field, data glyph)?\n- How should visitors manipulate or perceive it (static hero, orbit control, camera-relative movement)?\n- What level of hardware/performance do we target (mobile hero snippet vs. desktop interactive)?\n- Which animation best communicates the story (continuous rotation, bobbing, interaction-driven)?\n\n**Core principles**:\n1. **Scene graph first** – model hierarchy and transforms before materials.\n2. **Intent-driven primitives** – boxes, spheres, torus, planes cover 80% of hero cases; reach for GLTF only when fidelity demands it.\n3. **Animation as transformation** – treat animation as evolving position/rotation/scale with `renderer.setAnimationLoop`.\n4. **Performance through restraint** – reuse geometries/materials, clamp device pixel ratio, keep draw calls low.\n\n---\n\n## Foundational Principle: Lock a “Reference Frame Contract” First\n\nMost Three.js bugs are not “rendering bugs” — they’re **reference-frame bugs**: wrong origin, wrong up-axis assumption, wrong forward direction, wrong “ground = y=0” semantics, wrong color space, or wrong loading environment.\n\nTreat your scene like a contract you must prove once, then never violate:\n- **Axes**: which way is forward for gameplay, and how do models map to it?\n- **Anchors**: what does “on the ground” mean for each asset class?\n- **Units**: what is 1 unit (meter-ish? pixel-ish?) and how do imported assets fit?\n- **Color**: are textures and output color space correct?\n\nIf you don’t lock this contract early, you will chase symptoms: inverted movement, floating/sinking models, “wrongly loaded” textures, and end-state hangs caused by tangled state transitions.\n\n### The Calibration Pass (do this before building gameplay)\nDo a 60-second calibration scene and lock constants (axes/anchors/scale/color) before shipping gameplay systems.\n\nDeep guide + troubleshooting map: `references/reference-frame-contract.md`\n\n### Mesh Forward Verification (Do Not Guess)\nDon’t “eyeball rotate until it looks right” and don’t assume “GLTF faces `-Z`”.\n\nIn the calibration scene, **prove** each imported model’s forward direction and lock it as a constant (global `MODEL_YAW_OFFSET` or per-asset `yawOffset`).\n\nIf you want a reusable helper module instead of hand-rolling arrows/box helpers each time:\n- Install (repo-scoped): run `python3 .codex/skills/threejs-builder/scripts/install-gltf-calibration-helpers.py --out ./gltf-calibration-helpers.mjs`\n- Install (from within the skill folder): run `python3 scripts/install-gltf-calibration-helpers.py --out ./gltf-calibration-helpers.mjs`\n- Use: import and call `attachGltfCalibrationHelpers(...)` (see `scripts/README.md`)\n\nMinimal check:\n```js\n// In Three.js, an Object3D’s \"forward\" is its local -Z axis.\nconst localForward = new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, -1);\n\n// Attach a visible arrow to the model so you can *see* its forward.\nconst forwardArrow = new THREE.ArrowHelper(localForward, new THREE.Vector3(0, 1.2, 0), 1.2, 0xff00ff);\nmodelRoot.add(forwardArrow);\n\n// Also log the current world-forward for debugging (post-normalization and post-rotation).\nconst worldForward = new THREE.Vector3();\nmodelRoot.getWorldDirection(worldForward);\nconsole.log(''model world forward (-Z):'', worldForward.toArray());\n```\n\nThen decide:\n- If the mesh runs backward, set `yawOffset = Math.PI`.\n- If it faces the camera (common symptom), your yaw convention is wrong—flip the offset and re-check.\n\n## Coordinate System & Camera Awareness (Critical)\n\nThree.js is right-handed: +X right, +Y up, +Z toward the camera. Many GLTF assets are authored facing `-Z`, but **verify per pack** (don’t assume). Camera-relative controls must project the camera forward vector onto the XZ plane, normalize, then derive the right vector via a right-handed cross product to avoid inverted WASD when the camera orbits.\n\n```\nconst forward = new THREE.Vector3();\ncamera.getWorldDirection(forward);\nforward.y = 0;\nforward.normalize();\n// Right-handed basis (DON''T swap arguments): right = forward × up\nconst right = new THREE.Vector3().crossVectors(forward, new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0));\n```\n\nPractical rule:\n- If A/D is inverted, your cross product order is wrong (or you need to flip `forward` with `forward.negate()` depending on your convention). Fix the basis, not the key mapping.\n\n---\n\n## Origins & “Ground” Anchors (Stop Guessing)\n\nAnchoring is an asset-contract decision, not a “tweak until it looks right” decision.\n\nRule of thumb:\n- Characters/props: `minY = 0`\n- Ground tiles: often `maxY = 0` (walkable surface)\n\nDeep guide + example code: `references/reference-frame-contract.md`\n\n---\n\n## Build Flow\n\n### 1. Frame the Experience\n- Define the vibe (portfolio, gamey, data viz) and jot a mini mood board (colors, light style, animation verbs).\n- Choose interaction tier: static render, auto-rotation, OrbitControls, or custom camera/gameplay loop.\n- Sketch layout: do you need a ground plane, backdrop gradient, floating particles, or spotlight object?\n\n### 2. Establish Runtime Foundations\n- Use modern ES modules—no global `THREE`. Import from `three` package or CDN versions (>=0.150).\n- Minimal HTML template:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Three.js Scene</title>\n  <style>body{margin:0;overflow:hidden;background:#010103;}canvas{display:block;}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <script type=\"module\">\n    import * as THREE from ''https://unpkg.com/three@0.160.0/build/three.module.js'';\n\n    const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n    const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(60, innerWidth / innerHeight, 0.1, 2000);\n    camera.position.set(0, 1.5, 4.5);\n\n    const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });\n    renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));\n    renderer.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\n    document.body.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n    window.addEventListener(''resize'', () => {\n      camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n      camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n      renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n- Plug OrbitControls from `three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js` when interaction is needed, enable damping, and call `controls.update()` each frame.\n\n### 2.5 GLTF Loading Guardrails (When You Use Models)\n- Run via a local server (not `file://`) so relative resources resolve reliably.\n- For animated/skinned GLTF instancing, use `SkeletonUtils.clone()` (plain `.clone()` breaks skeleton links).\n- Always log animation clip names after load and select by exact string (avoid “best guess” name matching unless it’s a deliberate fallback).\n- If your asset pack uses an atlas, avoid “multiply tinting” materials (it can turn textured models into weird flat colors). Prefer leaving `material.color` at white and using emissive/lighting for emphasis.\n\n### 3. Compose the Scene\n- **Geometries**: prefer built-ins (Box, Sphere, Torus, Plane, Cone, Icosahedron). For particle clouds use `BufferGeometry` + `Float32Array` positions.\n- **Materials**: pick `MeshStandardMaterial` as default (tweak `roughness`/`metalness`), `MeshPhysicalMaterial` for glass/liquids, `MeshBasicMaterial` for unlit accents, `PointsMaterial` for particles.\n- **Lighting**: start with Ambient (0.3–0.5) + Directional key + colored fill; enable shadows only when necessary and set `renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true` + map sizes of 1024–2048.\n- **Color palettes**: define constants (e.g., `const COLORS = { primary: 0xff6600, accent: 0x0ff0ff }`) and keep backgrounds dark to let emissive tones pop.\n\n### 4. Animate & Interact\n- Implement animation loops with `renderer.setAnimationLoop((time) => { ... renderer.render(scene, camera); });`.\n- Common patterns:\n  - Continuous rotation with `mesh.rotation.y = time * 0.001`.\n  - Bobbing via `mesh.position.y = Math.sin(time * 0.002) * 0.4`.\n  - Mouse-reactive tilt: normalize pointer coords and lerp rotations for smoothness.\n  - Camera-relative character motion for interactive demos (see snippet above for direction vectors).\n- Store state outside the loop (e.g., `const inputState = { up: false, ... }`).\n\n### 4.5 State Machines & “Time Ran Out” Bugs\nIf your app “hangs” at time-out, it’s almost always because multiple systems are competing to transition state.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Use a single `state.mode` and a single transition function.\n- Treat `timeLeft <= 0` as terminal and clamp it once: `timeLeft = Math.max(0, timeLeft - dt)`.\n- Add a one-way latch like `hasEnded` so the end transition can only happen once.\n\n### 5. Polish & Performance\n- Cap `renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2))` to keep 4K laptops smooth.\n- Reuse geometries/materials, avoid instantiating inside the animation loop.\n- Use helpers (GridHelper, AxesHelper) for debugging, but remove them for production scenes.\n- Separate setup helpers (e.g., `createLights()`/`createMeshes()`) to keep files navigable.\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n❌ **Legacy global builds**: Using `<script src=\"three.js\"></script>` and accessing `THREE` globals breaks tree-shaking and OrbitControls imports. Use ES modules.\n\n❌ **Camera-blind controls**: Mapping WASD directly to world axes feels wrong once the camera rotates. Always derive movement vectors from the camera orientation.\n\n❌ **Floating/sinking fixes by “random y offsets”**: If you’re tweaking `position.y` in 5 places, your anchoring strategy is missing.\nWhy bad: you’ll never converge across ground tiles vs characters vs props.\nBetter: normalize each asset to a declared anchor (`minY` or `maxY`) at load time and only place the wrapper.\n\n❌ **Asset guessing**: Assuming GLTF forward direction, scale, or animation names without a calibration pass.\nBetter: build a 60-second calibration scene and lock constants (forward offsets, anchors, heights).\n\n❌ **Off-center canvases from transform math**: Mixing `translate()` + `scale()` with the wrong `transform-origin` makes the render area drift.\nBetter: center via layout (flex/grid) and apply `scale()` only, with `transform-origin: center`.\n\n❌ **Geometry churn inside loops**: Creating geometries/materials each frame tanks GC and FPS. Instantiate once and mutate transforms only.\n\n❌ **Overly dense primitives**: Jumping to `SphereGeometry(1, 128, 128)` without purpose wastes perf; start with defaults and scale segments only when silhouetted edges demand it.\n\n❌ **Unbounded pixel ratio**: Forgetting to clamp `devicePixelRatio` makes retina users suffer. Always clamp to ≤2 unless photorealism is mandatory.\n\n---\n\n## Variation Guidance\n\n- **Purpose-specific styling**:\n  - Portfolio hero → slow easing, glossy lighting, analogous palettes.\n  - Game prototype → punchy colors, contrasty lights, camera-relative controls, particles.\n  - Data viz → clean planes, grid helpers, consistent units, annotations.\n  - Background loop → subtle gradients, low-frequency motion, ambient glow.\n- **Mix geometry/material** choices: cycle through spheres, rounded boxes, low-poly icosahedrons, tubes. Experiment with `flatShading`, `wireframe`, emissive blooms.\n- **Camera moods**: alternate between dolly-in hero (z≈4), aerial tilt (camera.set(8, 11, -6)), or isometric (45° yaw). Pair with matching movement logic.\n- **Animation verbs**: rotate, pulse, orbit, flock, noise-driven drift. Avoid always rotating cubes at `0.001` speed.\n\n---\n\n## Remember\n\nThree.js scenes succeed when the mental model (scene graph + intent) guides the build. Lead with philosophy, respect the coordinate system, keep loops lean, and vary geometry, lighting, and animation so every experience feels purpose-built. Let these patterns unlock creativity—they are rails, not cages.\n\nFor specific topics, see the **Reference Files** table at the top of this document.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:03:34.071Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing advanced 3D web experience development with Three.js and modern ES modules.","zh":"非常适合需要利用 Three.js 和现代 ES 模块开发高级 3D Web 体验的 AI Agent。","ja":"Three.js と最新の ES モジュールを使用した高度な 3D Web エクスペリエンスの開発を必要とする AI Agent に最適です。","ko":"Three.js와 현대적인 ES 모듈을 사용하여 고급 3D 웹 경험을 개발해야 하는 AI 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Ideal para AI Agents que necesitan desarrollar experiencias web en 3D avanzadas con Three.js y módulos ES modernos.","fr":"Parfait pour les AI Agents nécessitant le développement d''expériences web 3D avancées avec Three.js et des modules ES modernes.","de":"Perfekt für AI Agents, die fortgeschrittene 3D-Web-Erfahrungen mit Three.js und modernen ES-Modulen entwickeln müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de desenvolvimento avançado de experiências web em 3D com Three.js e módulos ES modernos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-агентов, которым требуется разработка продвинутых 3D веб-экспериментов с Three.js и современными ES-модулями.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى تطوير تجارب ويب ثلاثية الأبعاد متقدمة باستخدام Three.js ووحدات ES الحديثة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build elegant, performant Three.js web experiences with support for GLTF models, reference frames, and SkeletonUtils, utilizing Codex CLI and modern ES modules for seamless integration.","zh":"赋能 Agent 利用 Codex CLI 和现代 ES 模块实现无缝集成，构建支持 GLTF 模型、参考帧和 SkeletonUtils 的优雅且高性能的 Three.js Web 体验。","ja":"Codex CLI と最新の ES モジュールを活用したシームレスな統合により、GLTF モデル、リファレンスフレーム、SkeletonUtils をサポートする、エレガントで高性能な Three.js Web エクスペリエンスを構築する能力を Agent に提供します。","ko":"Codex CLI와 현대적인 ES 모듈을 활용한 원활한 통합을 통해, GLTF 모델, 참조 프레임 및 SkeletonUtils를 지원하는 우아하고 고성능의 Three.js 웹 경험을 구축할 수 있는 능력을 에이전트에게 부여합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes construir experiencias web elegantes y de alto rendimiento con Three.js, con soporte para modelos GLTF, reference frames y SkeletonUtils, utilizando Codex CLI y módulos ES modernos para una integración perfecta.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des expériences web élégantes et performantes avec Three.js, avec prise en charge des modèles GLTF, des reference frames et de SkeletonUtils, en utilisant Codex CLI et des modules ES modernes pour une intégration transparente.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, elegante und leistungsstarke Three.js-Web-Erfahrungen mit Unterstützung für GLTF-Modelle, reference frames und SkeletonUtils zu erstellen, unter Verwendung von Codex CLI und modernen ES-Modulen für nahtlose Integration.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a construir experiências web elegantes e de alto desempenho com Three.js, com suporte para modelos GLTF, referenciais e SkeletonUtils, utilizando Codex CLI e módulos ES modernos para uma integração perfeita.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать элегантные и производительные веб-эксперименты на Three.js с поддержкой моделей GLTF, систем отсчета и SkeletonUtils, используя Codex CLI и современные ES-модули для беспрепятственной интеграции.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من بناء تجارب ويب أنيقة وعالية الأداء باستخدام Three.js مع دعم لنماذج GLTF، وأطر المرجعية، و SkeletonUtils، مستخدمين Codex CLI ووحدات ES الحديثة لتحقيق تكامل سلس."},"useCases":{"en":["Loading and caching 3D models with GLTF","Calibrating and anchoring reference frames for accurate axis correctness","Debugging Three.js web experiences with comprehensive reference guides"],"zh":["使用 GLTF 加载和缓存 3D 模型","校准和锚定参考帧以确保轴精度","使用全面的参考指南调试 Three.js Web 体验"],"ja":["GLTF を使用した 3D モデルの読み込みとキャッシュ","正確な軸精度のためのリファレンスフレームのキャリブレーションとアンカー設定","包括的なリファレンスガイドを使用した Three.js Web エクスペリエンスのデバッグ"],"ko":["GLTF를 사용한 3D 모델 로딩 및 캐싱","정확한 축 정확성을 위한 참조 프레임 보정 및 고정","포괄적인 참조 가이드를 사용한 Three.js 웹 경험 디버깅"],"es":["Carga y almacenamiento en caché de modelos 3D con GLTF","Calibración y anclaje de reference frames para una corrección precisa de ejes","Depuración de experiencias web con Three.js utilizando guías de referencia completas"],"fr":["Chargement et mise en cache de modèles 3D avec GLTF","Calibrage et ancrage des reference frames pour une précision d''axe exacte","Débogage d''expériences web Three.js avec des guides de référence complets"],"de":["Laden und Caching von 3D-Modellen mit GLTF","Kalibrieren und Verankern von reference frames für eine genaue Achsenkorrektheit","Debuggen von Three.js-Web-Erfahrungen mit umfassenden Referenzhandbüchern"],"pt":["Carregar e armazenar em cache modelos 3D com GLTF","Calibrar e ancorar referenciais para correção precisa dos eixos","Depurar experiências web com Three.js usando guias de referência abrangentes"],"ru":["Загрузка и кэширование 3D-моделей с использованием GLTF","Калибровка и привязка систем отсчета для обеспечения точной корректности осей","Отладка веб-экспериментов на Three.js с использованием комплексных руководств"],"ar":["تحميل ونماذج التخزين المؤقت ثلاثية الأبعاد باستخدام GLTF","معايرة وتثبيت أطر المرجعية لضمان دقة المحور الصحيحة","تصحيح أخطاء تجارب الويب باستخدام Three.js مع أدلة مرجعية شاملة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Codex CLI for integration","Specific to Three.js and modern ES modules","Needs reference to specific guide files for topics like GLTF models and reference frames"],"zh":["集成需要 Codex CLI","特定于 Three.js 和现代 ES 模块","需要参考特定的指南文件以了解诸如 GLTF 模型和参考帧等主题"],"ja":["統合には Codex CLI が必要","Three.js と最新の ES モジュールに特化","GLTF モデルやリファレンスフレームなどのトピックについては、特定のガイドファイルを参照する必要がある"],"ko":["통합에는 Codex CLI가 필요함","Three.js 및 현대적인 ES 모듈에 특화됨","GLTF 모델 및 참조 프레임과 같은 주제에 대해 특정 가이드 파일을 참조해야 함"],"es":["Requiere Codex CLI para la integración","Específico para Three.js y módulos ES modernos","Necesita referencia a archivos de guía específicos para temas como modelos GLTF y reference frames"],"fr":["Nécessite Codex CLI pour l''intégration","Spécifique à Three.js et aux modules ES modernos","Nécessite une référence à des fichiers guides spécifiques pour des sujets tels que les modèles GLTF et les reference frames"],"de":["Erfordert Codex CLI für die Integration","Spezifisch für Three.js und moderne ES-Module","Benötigt Referenz auf spezifische Handbuchdateien für Themen wie GLTF-Modelle und reference frames"],"pt":["Requer Codex CLI para integração","Específico para Three.js e módulos ES modernos","Necessita de referência a arquivos de guia específicos para tópicos como modelos GLTF e referenciais"],"ru":["Требует Codex CLI для интеграции","Специфично для Three.js и современных ES-модулей","Требует об